ameter services required for each supported tax year\nweb test:native-pair: + * the canonical calculator ID, jurisdiction and tax-year literals\nweb test:native-pair: + * expected errors and validation help\nweb test:native-pair: + * API and SDK compatibility impact\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Implementation [#implementation]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Keep the calculator small. It should require facts and return a schema-backed\nweb test:native-pair: + report. Rule layers should derive tax facts.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`txt\nweb test:native-pair: + accepted input facts\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> scenario layer\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> official rule pack layer\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> calculator program\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> schema-backed report\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Do not place calculator business logic in \\`@taxkit/api-http\\` handlers, SDK\nweb test:native-pair: + helpers or docs-only examples. HTTP and SDK layers must call the canonical\nweb test:native-pair: + calculator boundary and preserve \\`CalculatorRun*\\` contracts.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Tests [#tests]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Your evidence should include:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * golden tests for the calculator output\nweb test:native-pair: + * graph validation for every required and provided fact\nweb test:native-pair: + * schema decode tests for calculator input and report schemas\nweb test:native-pair: + * type tests for SDK descriptor inference\nweb test:native-pair: + * API compatibility tests for \\`POST /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/calculate\\`\nweb test:native-pair: + * SDK compatibility tests for \\`TaxKit.calculate\\`, \\`TaxKit.safe.calculate\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +   and any jurisdiction helper such as \\`au.incomeTax.annual\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Pull request evidence [#pull-request-evidence]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Attach source citations, test output, compatibility notes and a Changeset or\nweb test:native-pair: + no-Changeset rationale in [PR evidence checklist](/contributing/pr-evidence-checklist).\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`add-a-calculator`,content:`Use this guide when you need a new public calculation goal or report, such as\nweb test:native-pair: + a new withholding, annual tax or repayment calculation.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Read Calculators.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Read the public boundary in\nweb test:native-pair: + API and SDK.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:\"Inspect the calculator catalogue in `@taxkit/calculators`.\"},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:\"The rule package owns the calculator program, report schema and rule-pack\\nlayer. `@taxkit/calculators` owns reusable catalogue entries,\\n`CalculatorRunRequest`, `CalculatorRunResponse`, `CalculatorServiceError`,\\nmetadata projections, graph construction and service execution.\"},{heading:`proposal`,content:`Describe:`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the calculation goal and report fields`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the accepted input facts and scenario context`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the rule packs and parameter services required for each supported tax year`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the canonical calculator ID, jurisdiction and tax-year literals`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`expected errors and validation help`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`API and SDK compatibility impact`},{heading:`implementation`,content:`Keep the calculator small. It should require facts and return a schema-backed\nweb test:native-pair: + report. Rule layers should derive tax facts.`},{heading:`implementation`,content:\"Do not place calculator business logic in `@taxkit/api-http` handlers, SDK\\nhelpers or docs-only examples. HTTP and SDK layers must call the canonical\\ncalculator boundary and preserve `CalculatorRun*` contracts.\"},{heading:`tests`,content:`Your evidence should include:`},{heading:`tests`,content:`golden tests for the calculator output`},{heading:`tests`,content:`graph validation for every required and provided fact`},{heading:`tests`,content:`schema decode tests for calculator input and report schemas`},{heading:`tests`,content:`type tests for SDK descriptor inference`},{heading:`tests`,content:\"API compatibility tests for `POST /api/v1/calculators/:calculatorId/calculate`\"},{heading:`tests`,content:\"SDK compatibility tests for `TaxKit.calculate`, `TaxKit.safe.calculate`\\nand any jurisdiction helper such as `au.incomeTax.annual`\"},{heading:`pull-request-evidence`,content:`Attach source citations, test output, compatibility notes and a Changeset or\nweb test:native-pair: + no-Changeset rationale in PR evidence checklist.`}],headings:[{id:`add-a-calculator`,content:`Add a calculator`},{id:`before-you-start`,content:`Before you start`},{id:`proposal`,content:`Proposal`},{id:`implementation`,content:`Implementation`},{id:`tests`,content:`Tests`},{id:`pull-request-evidence`,content:`Pull request evidence`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#add-a-calculator`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Add a calculator`})},{depth:2,url:`#before-you-start`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Before you start`})},{depth:2,url:`#proposal`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Proposal`})},{depth:2,url:`#implementation`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Implementation`})},{depth:2,url:`#tests`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Tests`})},{depth:2,url:`#pull-request-evidence`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Pull request evidence`})}];function o(e){let n={a:`a`,code:`code`,h1:`h1`,h2:`h2`,li:`li`,p:`p`,pre:`pre`,span:`span`,ul:`ul`,...e.components};return(0,t.jsxs)(t.Fragment,{children:[(0,t.jsx)(n.h1,{id:`add-a-calculator`,children:`Add a calculator`}),`\nweb test:native-pai