\nweb test:native-pair: + Rule packages own tax-year parameter tables and rule-pack composition.\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`@taxkit/core\\` owns the shared \\`TaxYear\\` brand and\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`australianTaxYearInterval\\`. Rule packages narrow that brand to supported\nweb test:native-pair: + literals such as \\`AuPayTaxYear\\` or \\`AuAnnualTaxYear\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Proposal [#proposal]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Document:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * the official source for each table or rate\nweb test:native-pair: + * the effective start and end dates\nweb test:native-pair: + * the calculator IDs and jurisdictions the year supports\nweb test:native-pair: + * the parameter service that owns each table\nweb test:native-pair: + * expected differences from the previous year\nweb test:native-pair: + * release impact for API metadata and SDK descriptors\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Implementation [#implementation]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Add tax-year data as schema-validated parameters. Compose it into the owning\nweb test:native-pair: + rule pack and calculator catalogue only after golden tests prove the year.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`txt\nweb test:native-pair: + official source\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> parameter table schema\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> parameter descriptor with effective period\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> rule-pack layer\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> calculator catalogue entry\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> API and SDK metadata\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Do not default missing request context to a jurisdiction or tax year in HTTP,\nweb test:native-pair: + SDK or calculator service code. Missing context must be absent, schema-owned\nweb test:native-pair: + or rejected with a tagged expected error.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Tests [#tests]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Your evidence should include:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * parameter schema validation\nweb test:native-pair: + * source reference validation\nweb test:native-pair: + * effective-date overlap checks\nweb test:native-pair: + * golden tests for the new tax year\nweb test:native-pair: + * date-boundary tests around year start and end\nweb test:native-pair: + * API compatibility tests proving metadata lists the year\nweb test:native-pair: + * SDK compatibility tests proving unsupported tax-year literals still fail\nweb test:native-pair: +   type tests\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Pull request evidence [#pull-request-evidence]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Include source citations, changed parameter periods, commands and release\nweb test:native-pair: + impact in [PR evidence checklist](/contributing/pr-evidence-checklist).\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`add-a-tax-year`,content:`Use this guide when a supported calculator needs a new official tax year,\nweb test:native-pair: + parameter period or date boundary.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Read Rules and parameters.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Read Calculators.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Check the current supported tax years in\nweb test:native-pair: + Jurisdictions and tax years.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:\"Rule packages own tax-year parameter tables and rule-pack composition.\\n`@taxkit/core` owns the shared `TaxYear` brand and\\n`australianTaxYearInterval`. Rule packages narrow that brand to supported\\nliterals such as `AuPayTaxYear` or `AuAnnualTaxYear`.\"},{heading:`proposal`,content:`Document:`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the official source for each table or rate`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the effective start and end dates`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the calculator IDs and jurisdictions the year supports`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`the parameter service that owns each table`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`expected differences from the previous year`},{heading:`proposal`,content:`release impact for API metadata and SDK descriptors`},{heading:`implementation`,content:`Add tax-year data as schema-validated parameters. Compose it into the owning\nweb test:native-pair: + rule pack and calculator catalogue only after golden tests prove the year.`},{heading:`implementation`,content:`Do not default missing request context to a jurisdiction or tax year in HTTP,\nweb test:native-pair: + SDK or calculator service code. Missing context must be absent, schema-owned\nweb test:native-pair: + or rejected with a tagged expected error.`},{heading:`tests`,content:`Your evidence should include:`},{heading:`tests`,content:`parameter schema validation`},{heading:`tests`,content:`source reference validation`},{heading:`tests`,content:`effective-date overlap checks`},{heading:`tests`,content:`golden tests for the new tax year`},{heading:`tests`,content:`date-boundary tests around year start and end`},{heading:`tests`,content:`API compatibility tests proving metadata lists the year`},{heading:`tests`,content:`SDK compatibility tests proving unsupported tax-year literals still fail\nweb test:native-pair: + type tests`},{heading:`pull-request-evidence`,content:`Include source citations, changed parameter periods, commands and release\nweb test:native-pair: + impact in PR evidence checklist.`}],headings:[{id:`add-a-tax-year`,content:`Add a tax year`},{id:`before-you-start`,content:`Before you start`},{id:`proposal`,content:`Proposal`},{id:`implementation`,content:`Implementation`},{id:`tests`,content:`Tests`},{id:`pull-request-evidence`,content:`Pull request evidence`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#add-a-tax-year`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Add a tax year`})},{depth:2,url:`#before-you-start`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Before you start`})},{dep