tions [#review-expectations]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use this page when you want to know how a maintainer will review a\nweb test:native-pair: + contribution.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## What reviewers check [#what-reviewers-check]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Reviewers check:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * the contribution is routed to the owning package\nweb test:native-pair: + * source citations prove the changed tax behaviour\nweb test:native-pair: + * facts, rules, calculators and tax years use canonical schemas and branded\nweb test:native-pair: +   IDs\nweb test:native-pair: + * HTTP and SDK layers do not hide tax business logic\nweb test:native-pair: + * golden tests, type tests, API compatibility tests and SDK compatibility\nweb test:native-pair: +   tests match the changed surface\nweb test:native-pair: + * expected errors use canonical tagged errors such as \\`CalculatorServiceError\\`\nweb test:native-pair: + * optional policy uses schema-owned fields, \\`Option\\` and \\`Match\\`\nweb test:native-pair: + * public docs use current names and avoid stale aliases\nweb test:native-pair: + * release-impact notes and Changesets are correct\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Documentation review [#documentation-review]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + When docs change, reviewers also check:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * second person voice\nweb test:native-pair: + * Australian spelling\nweb test:native-pair: + * sentence-case headings\nweb test:native-pair: + * no marketing language\nweb test:native-pair: + * links resolve to the source of truth\nweb test:native-pair: + * diagrams clarify a decision, ownership path or validation flow\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Read [Documentation review](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/docs/standards/documentation-review.md)\nweb test:native-pair: + for the full audit checklist.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Return requests [#return-requests]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + A reviewer may ask you to update the PR when evidence is missing, ownership is\nweb test:native-pair: + wrong, a public contract changed without compatibility notes or tax behaviour\nweb test:native-pair: + appears in HTTP, SDK or docs-only code.\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`review-expectations`,content:`Use this page when you want to know how a maintainer will review a\nweb test:native-pair: + contribution.`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`Reviewers check:`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`the contribution is routed to the owning package`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`source citations prove the changed tax behaviour`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`facts, rules, calculators and tax years use canonical schemas and branded\nweb test:native-pair: + IDs`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`HTTP and SDK layers do not hide tax business logic`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`golden tests, type tests, API compatibility tests and SDK compatibility\nweb test:native-pair: + tests match the changed surface`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:\"expected errors use canonical tagged errors such as `CalculatorServiceError`\"},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:\"optional policy uses schema-owned fields, `Option` and `Match`\"},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`public docs use current names and avoid stale aliases`},{heading:`what-reviewers-check`,content:`release-impact notes and Changesets are correct`},{heading:`documentation-review`,content:`When docs change, reviewers also check:`},{heading:`documentation-review`,content:`second person voice`},{heading:`documentation-review`,content:`Australian spelling`},{heading:`documentation-review`,content:`sentence-case headings`},{headi