t:native-pair: + Use SDK schema exports when your application needs the canonical calculator run\nweb test:native-pair: + contracts or safe-result error shapes.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Import schemas [#import-schemas]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import {\nweb test:native-pair: +   CalculatorRunFacts,\nweb test:native-pair: +   CalculatorRunRequest,\nweb test:native-pair: +   CalculatorRunResponse,\nweb test:native-pair: +   CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\nweb test:native-pair: +   CalculatorServiceError,\nweb test:native-pair: + } from \"@taxkit/sdk/schemas\";\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + These names are re-exported from the calculator package for consumer\nweb test:native-pair: + convenience. The calculator package remains the source of truth for the\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`CalculatorRun*\\` contracts and \\`CalculatorServiceError\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Common contracts [#common-contracts]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + | Name                          | Use                                           |\nweb test:native-pair: + | ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRunFacts\\`          | Canonical facts accepted by calculator runs.  |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRunRequest\\`        | Public calculator run payload shape.          |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRunServiceRequest\\` | Service-level request with the calculator id. |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRunResponse\\`       | Canonical run response shape.                 |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorServiceError\\`      | Expected calculator service failure union.    |\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Safe-result schemas [#safe-result-schemas]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + The SDK also exports safe-result and error schemas:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import {\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitClientDisposedError,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitClientDisposeError,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitFailure,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitSchemaDecodeError,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitSuccess,\nweb test:native-pair: + } from \"@taxkit/sdk/schemas\";\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use these when you persist, inspect or validate results returned by\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`TaxKit.safe.calculate\\`. \\`TaxKitClientDisposedError\\` describes calculation calls\nweb test:native-pair: + after a client closes. \\`TaxKitClientDisposeError\\` describes a safe cleanup failure\nweb test:native-pair: + from \\`dispose()\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Related pages [#related-pages]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Safe SDK](/sdk/safe-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Effect SDK](/sdk/effect-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Type safety](/sdk/type-safety)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`schemas`,content:`Use SDK schema exports when your application needs the canonical calculator run\nweb test:native-pair: + contracts or safe-result error shapes.`},{heading:`import-schemas`,content:\"These names are re-exported from the calculator package for consumer\\nconvenience. The calculator package remains the source of truth for the\\n`CalculatorRun*` contracts and `CalculatorServiceError`.\"},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Name`},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Use`},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:\"`CalculatorRunFacts`\"},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Canonical facts accepted by calculator runs.`},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:\"`CalculatorRunRequest`\"},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Public calculator run payload shape.`},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:\"`CalculatorRunServiceRequest`\"},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Service-level request with the calculator id.`},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:\"`CalculatorRunResponse`\"},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Canonical run response shape.`},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:\"`CalculatorServiceError`\"},{heading:`common-contracts`,content:`Expected calculator service failure union.`},{heading:`safe-result-schemas`,content:`The SDK also exports safe-result and error schemas:`},{heading:`safe-result-schemas`,content:\"Use these when you persist, inspect or validate results returned by\\n`TaxKit.safe.calculate`. `TaxKitClientDisposedError` describes calculation calls\\nafter a client closes. `TaxKitClientDisposeError` describes a safe cleanup failure\\nfrom `dispose()`.\"},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Safe SDK`},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Effect SDK`},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Type safety`}],headings:[{id:`schemas`,content:`Schemas`},{id:`import-schemas`,content:`Import schemas`},{id:`common-contracts`,content:`Common contracts`},{id:`safe-result-schemas`,content:`Safe-result schemas`},{id:`related-pages`,content:`Related pages`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#schemas`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Schemas`})},{depth:2,url:`#import-schemas`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Import schemas`})},{depth:2,url:`#common-contracts`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Common contracts`})},{depth:2,url:`#safe-result-schemas`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Safe-result schemas`})},{depth:2,url:`#related-pages`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Related pages`})}];function o(e){let n={a:`a`,code:`code`,h1:`h1`,h2:`h2`,li:`li`,p:`p`,pre:`pre`,span:`span`,table:`table`,tbody:`tbody`,td:`td`,th:`th`,thead:`thead`,tr:`tr`,ul:`ul`,...e.components};return(0,t.jsxs)(t.Fragment,{children:[(0,t.jsx)(n.h1,{id:`schemas`,children:`Schemas`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.p,{children:`Use SDK sch