u want Australian calculator helpers and descriptors.                                                     |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`@taxkit/sdk/effect\\`  | You want \\`calculateRunRequest\\`, \\`calculateReportRequest\\`, \\`calculateReport\\` or Effect service requirements. |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`@taxkit/sdk/schemas\\` | You want \\`CalculatorRunRequest\\`, \\`CalculatorRunResponse\\`, \\`CalculatorServiceError\\` and SDK result schemas.  |\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Beginner path [#beginner-path]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + const report = await au.incomeTax.annual({\nweb test:native-pair: +   taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Australian helpers keep the first calculation compact while still using the\nweb test:native-pair: + same descriptor and schema contracts as the generic SDK facade.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Generic path [#generic-path]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { TaxKit } from \"@taxkit/sdk\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + const report = await TaxKit.calculate(au.calculations.annualIncomeTax, {\nweb test:native-pair: +   taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Advanced Effect path [#advanced-effect-path]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use the Effect SDK when you want to provide \\`PublicCalculatorService\\` through\nweb test:native-pair: + your own Effect layer or when an in-process transport needs the full\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`CalculatorRunResponse\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import { calculateRunRequest } from \"@taxkit/sdk/effect\";\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Next steps [#next-steps]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * Read [Plain SDK](/sdk/plain-sdk) for Promise-based usage.\nweb test:native-pair: + * Read [Safe SDK](/sdk/safe-sdk) for typed success and failure results.\nweb test:native-pair: + * Read [Effect SDK](/sdk/effect-sdk) for service composition.\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`typescript-sdk`,content:`Use the TypeScript SDK when your application can run TaxKit calculations\nweb test:native-pair: + in-process. The plain facade is the beginner path. The safe facade returns\nweb test:native-pair: + typed result values. The Effect facade is for advanced service composition and\nweb test:native-pair: + in-process transports.`},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:`Entrypoint`},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:`Use when`},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"`@taxkit/sdk`\"},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"You want `TaxKit.calculate`, `TaxKit.safe.calculate` or `TaxKit.createClient`.\"},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"`@taxkit/sdk/au`\"},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:`You want Australian calculator helpers and descriptors.`},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"`@taxkit/sdk/effect`\"},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"You want `calculateRunRequest`, `calculateReportRequest`, `calculateReport` or Effect service requirements.\"},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"`@taxkit/sdk/schemas`\"},{heading:`entrypoints`,content:\"You want `CalculatorRunRequest`, `CalculatorRunResponse`, `CalculatorServiceError` and SDK result schemas.\"},{heading:`beginner-path`,content:`Australian helpers keep the first calculation compact while still using the\nweb test:native-pair: + same descriptor and schema contracts as the generic SDK facade.`},{heading:`advanced-effect-path`,content:\"Use the Effect SDK when you want to provide `PublicCalculatorService` through\\nyour own Effect layer or when an in-process transport needs the full\\n`CalculatorRunResponse`.\"},{heading:`next-steps`,content:`Read Plain SDK for Promise-based usage.`},{heading:`next-steps`,content:`Read Safe SDK for typed success and failure results.`},{heading:`next-steps`,content:`Read Effect SDK for service composition.`}],headings:[{id:`typescript-sdk`,content:`TypeScript SDK`},{id:`entrypoints`,content:`Entrypoints`},{id:`beginner-path`,content:`Beginner path`},{id:`generic-path`,content:`Generic path`},{id:`advanced-effect-path`,content:`Advanced Effect path`},{id:`next-steps`,content:`Next steps`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#typescript-sdk`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`TypeScript SDK`})},{depth:2,url:`#entrypoints`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Entrypoints`})},{depth:2,url:`#beginner-path`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Beginner path`})},{depth:2,url:`#generic-path`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Generic path`})},{depth:2,url:`#advanced-effect-path`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Advanced Effect path`})},{depth:2,url:`#next-steps`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Next steps`})}];function o(e){let n={a:`a`,code:`code`,h1:`h1`,h2:`h2`,li:`li`,p:`p`,pre:`pre`,span:`span`,table:`table`,tbody:`tbody`,td:`td`,th:`th`,thead:`thead`,tr:`tr`,ul:`ul`,...e.components};return(0,t.jsxs)(t.Fragment,{children:[(0,t.jsx)(n.h1,{id:`typescript-sdk`,children:`TypeScript SDK`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.p,{children:`Use the TypeScript SDK when your application can run TaxKit calculations\nweb test:native-pair: + in-process. The plain facade is the beginner path. The safe facade returns\nweb test:native-pair: + typed result values. The Effect facade is for advanced serv