l it.`,status:`published`,title:`Authentication and deployment assumptions`},r=`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + # Authentication and deployment assumptions [#authentication-and-deployment-assumptions]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use this page before wiring a public client to the HTTP API. It records the\nweb test:native-pair: + current deployment assumptions without turning them into a field-level endpoint\nweb test:native-pair: + reference.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Current assumptions [#current-assumptions]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + The API app is \\`apps/api\\`. It serves the reusable HTTP contract from\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`@taxkit/api-http\\`. The standalone process uses \\`127.0.0.1:4000\\` by default;\nweb test:native-pair: + the native local API and website pair has addresses supplied by its launcher.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + There is no public authentication contract in this documentation slice. Treat\nweb test:native-pair: + authentication, tenant routing and public hosting as application-owned until a\nweb test:native-pair: + future API deployment spec defines them.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Local routes [#local-routes]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + For the native API and website pair, run \\`bun run dev\\` from the repository\nweb test:native-pair: + root. The launcher prints both local addresses. See the\nweb test:native-pair: + [API app README](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/apps/api/README.md) for this route and its build\nweb test:native-pair: + requirements.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + For the retained standalone API process, use:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`sh\nweb test:native-pair: + bun run --filter=api start\nweb test:native-pair: + curl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/health\nweb test:native-pair: + curl http://127.0.0.1:4000/api/docs/openapi.json\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + To run that standalone process through Portless, use:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`sh\nweb test:native-pair: + bun run --filter=api dev\nweb test:native-pair: + curl https://api.taxkit.localhost/api/health\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Caller responsibilities [#caller-responsibilities]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * Send \\`content-type: application/json\\` for calculate requests.\nweb test:native-pair: + * Pass canonical calculator facts in the request body.\nweb test:native-pair: + * Keep application authentication outside the calculator payload.\nweb test:native-pair: + * Read endpoint fields from the generated [OpenAPI reference](/api/openapi-reference).\nweb test:native-pair: + * Handle \\`CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope\\` for expected calculator service errors.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Related pages [#related-pages]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [API overview](/api/overview)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Endpoints](/api/endpoints)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Errors](/api/errors)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`authentication-and-deployment-assumptions`,content:`Use this page before wiring a public client to the HTTP API. It records the\nweb test:native-pair: + current deployment assumptions without turning them into a field-level endpoint\nweb test:native-pair: + reference.`},{heading:`current-assumptions`,content:\"The API app is `apps/api`. It serves the reusable HTTP contract from\\n`@taxkit/api-http`. The standalone process uses `127.0.0.1:4000` by default;\\nthe native local API and website pair has addresses supplied by its launcher.\"},{heading:`current-assumptions`,content:`There is no public authentication contract in this documentation slice. Treat\nweb test:native-pair: + authentication, tenant routing and public hosting as application-owned until a\nweb test:native-pair: + future API deployment spec defines them.`},{heading:`local-routes`,content:`For the native API and website pair, run \\`bun run dev\\` from the repository\nweb test:native-pair: + root. The launcher prints both local addresses. See the\nweb test:native-pair: + API app README for this route and its build\nweb test:native-pair: + requirements.`},{heading:`local-routes`,content:`For the retained standalone API process, use:`},{heading:`local-routes`,content:`To run that standalone process through Portless, use:`},{heading:`caller-responsibilities`,content:\"Send `content-type: application/json` for calculate requests.\"},{heading:`caller-responsibilities`,content:`Pass canonical calculator facts in the request body.`},{heading:`caller-responsibilities`,content:`Keep application authentication outside the calculator payload.`},{heading:`caller-responsibilities`,content:`Read endpoint fields from the generated OpenAPI reference.`},{heading:`caller-responsibilities`,content:\"Handle `CalculatorApiErrorEnvelope` for expected calculator service errors.\"},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`API overview`},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Endpoints`},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Errors`}],headings:[{id:`authentication-and-deployment-assumptions`,content:`Authentication and deployment assumptions`},{id:`current-assumptions`,content:`Current assumptions`},{id:`local-routes`,content:`Local routes`},{id:`caller-responsibilities`,content:`Caller responsibilities`},{id:`related-pages`,content:`Related pages`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#authentication-and-deployment-assumptions`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Authentication and deployment assumptions`})},{depth:2,url:`#current-assumptions`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Current assumptions`})},{depth:2,url:`#local-routes`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Local routes`})},{