 to run. It accepts canonical\nweb test:native-pair: + facts, composes the matching rules and returns a schema-backed report.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## When this matters [#when-this-matters]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Choose the calculator before you build a form, an API payload or a test. The\nweb test:native-pair: + selected calculator decides which facts are accepted and which report shape is\nweb test:native-pair: + returned.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## How it works [#how-it-works]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + CalculatorRunRequest\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> selected calculator catalog entry\nweb test:native-pair: +     -> canonical input fact schema decode\nweb test:native-pair: +     -> rule pack and parameter layers\nweb test:native-pair: +     -> report schema\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + For most TypeScript callers, use \\`au.incomeTax.annual\\` or\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`TaxKit.calculate\\`. For HTTP callers, pass the calculator ID in the route and\nweb test:native-pair: + the facts in the \\`CalculatorRunRequest\\` body.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Related concepts [#related-concepts]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Facts](/concepts/facts)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Rules](/concepts/rules)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Reports](/concepts/reports)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Calculators architecture](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/docs/architecture/calculators.md)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`calculators`,content:`A calculator is the public unit you ask TaxKit to run. It accepts canonical\nweb test:native-pair: + facts, composes the matching rules and returns a schema-backed report.`},{heading:`when-this-matters`,content:`Choose the calculator before you build a form, an API payload or a test. The\nweb test:native-pair: + selected calculator decides which facts are accepted and which report shape is\nweb test:native-pair: + returned.`},{heading:`how-it-works`,content:\"For most TypeScript callers, use `au.incomeTax.annual` or\\n`TaxKit.calculate`. For HTTP callers, pass the calculator ID in the route and\\nthe facts in the `CalculatorRunRequest` body.\"},{heading:`related-concepts`,content:`Facts`},{heading:`related-concepts`,content:`Rules`},{heading:`related-concepts`,content:`Reports`},{heading:`related-concepts`,content:`Calculators architecture`}],headings:[{id:`calculators`,content:`Calculators`},{id:`when-this-matters`,content:`When this matters`},{id:`how-it-works`,content:`How it works`},{id:`related-concepts`,content:`Related concepts`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#calculators`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Calculators`})},{depth:2,url:`#when-this-matters`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`When this matters`})},{depth:2,url:`#how-it-works`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`How it works`})},{depth:2,url:`#related-concepts`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Related concepts`})}];function o(e){let n={a:`a`,code:`code`,h1:`h1`,h2:`h2`,li:`li`,p:`p`,pre:`pre`,span:`span`,ul:`ul`,...e.components};return(0,t.jsxs)(t.Fragment,{children:[(0,t.jsx)(n.h1,{id:`calculators`,children:`Calculators`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.p,{children:`A calculator is the public unit you ask TaxKit to run. It accepts canonical\nweb test:native-pair: + facts, composes the matching rules and returns a schema-backed report.`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.h2,{id:`when-this-matters`,children:`When this matters`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.p,{children:`Choose the calculator before you build a form, an API payload or a test. The\nweb test:native-pair: + selected calculator decides which facts are accepted and which report shape is\nweb test:native-pair: + returned.`}),`\nweb test:nat