r: +\nweb test:native-pair: + The table describes the JSON form. In decoded TypeScript requests, context\nweb test:native-pair: + fields are nested Options: \\`None\\` for a missing key, \\`Some(None)\\` for a present\nweb test:native-pair: + undefined key, and \\`Some(Some(value))\\` for a value. Use the owning request\nweb test:native-pair: + constructor to supply defaults; do not send Option objects as raw HTTP JSON.\nweb test:native-pair: + The same rule applies to optional help/filter fields and returned optional\nweb test:native-pair: + question, help and duplicate-provider permission fields.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + The \\`facts\\` union is intentionally composed from canonical rule package\nweb test:native-pair: + schemas. Do not mirror request DTOs in application code when the SDK or API\nweb test:native-pair: + schema already owns the shape.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## CalculatorRunResponse [#calculatorrunresponse]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`CalculatorRunResponse\\` is the canonical full run response.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + | Field         | Type                     | Notes                                                                                               |\nweb test:native-pair: + | ------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`calculator\\`  | \\`CalculatorCatalogItem\\`  | Metadata for the selected calculator and context.                                                   |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`diagnostics\\` | \\`CalculationDiagnostics\\` | Graph and calculation diagnostics returned by the engine.                                           |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`report\\`      | \\`CalculatorRunReport\\`    | The calculator-specific report union. SDK helpers narrow this through the descriptor output schema. |\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## CalculatorServiceError [#calculatorserviceerror]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`CalculatorServiceError\\` is the expected calculator service failure union.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + | Error                               | When you see it                                                                                 |\nweb test:native-pair: + | ----------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorInputDecodeError\\`        | Request facts do not match the selected calculator input schema.                                |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`UnsupportedCalculatorError\\`        | The requested calculator id is not in the public catalogue.                                     |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`UnsupportedCalculatorContextError\\` | The calculator exists, but not for the requested jurisdiction or tax year.                      |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculationError\\`                  | The calculation engine returned a source-backed domain failure.                                 |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorCapacityExceeded\\`        | The server has no free calculation place. Retry manually after the current work finishes.       |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorOperationTimedOut\\`       | The operation reached its time limit. Retry manually.                                           |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRateLimited\\`             | The native per-client calculation limit was reached. Wait for \\`Retry-After\\` and retry manually. |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable\\`    | The native request identity or rate limiter is unavailable. Retry manually.                     |\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Runtime graph [#runtime-graph]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + Production: schema ownership\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + SDK or HTTP caller\nweb test:native-pair: +   -> CalculatorRunRequest\nweb test:native-pair: +     -> CalculatorRunFacts\nweb test:native-pair: +       -> rule-owned scenario input schema\nweb test:native-pair: +     -> PublicCalculatorService.calculate\nweb test:native-pair: +       -> CalculatorRunResponse\nweb test:native-pair: +       -> CalculatorServiceError for expected failures\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Owning sources [#owning-sources]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * Calculator schemas: [\\`packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts\\`](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts)\nweb test:native-pair: + * Calculator error projection: [\\`packages/calculators/src/errors.ts\\`](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/packages/calculators/src/errors.ts)\nweb test:native-pair: + * SDK schema re-exports: [\\`packages/sdk/typescript/src/schemas/index.ts\\`](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/packages/sdk/typescript/src/schemas/index.ts)\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Used by [#used-by]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Type safety](/sdk/type-safety)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [API errors](/api/errors)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Error reference](/reference/errors)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Examples](/reference/examples)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`schema-reference`,content:`Use this page when you need the canonical schema names for SDK, HTTP and test\nweb test:native-pair: + fixtures.`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"`CalculatorRunRequest` is the public request body schema for a calculator run.\\nIt is owned by `@taxkit/calculators`.\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`Field`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`Type`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`Notes`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"`facts`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"`CalculatorRunFacts`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`A union of rule-owned scenario input schemas.`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"`jurisdiction`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"optional `CalculatorJurisdiction`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`Omit only when the selected calculator has one supported context.`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"`taxYear`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"optional `CalculatorTaxYear`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`Omit only when the selected calculator has one supported tax year.`},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:\"The table describes the JSON form. In decoded TypeScript requests, context\\nfields are nested Options: `None` for a missing key, `Some(None)` for a present\\nundefined key, and `Some(Some(value))` for a value. Use the owning request\\nconstructor to supply defaults; do not send Option objects as raw HTTP JSON.\\nThe same rule applies to optional help/filter fields and returned optional\\nquestion, help and duplicate-provider permission fields.\"},{heading:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`The \\`facts\\` union is intentionally composed from canonical rule package\nweb test:native-pair: + schemas. Do not mirror request DTOs in application code when the SDK or API\nweb test:native-pair: + schema already owns the shape.`},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`CalculatorRunResponse` is the canonical full run response.\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`Field`},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`Type`},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`Notes`},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`calculator`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`CalculatorCatalogItem`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`Metadata for the selected calculator and context.`},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`diagnostics`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`CalculationDiagnostics`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`Graph and calculation diagnostics returned by the engine.`},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`report`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:\"`CalculatorRunReport`\"},{heading:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`The calculator-specific report union. SDK helpers narrow this through the descriptor output schema.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculatorServiceError` is the expected calculator service failure union.\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`Error`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`When you see it`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculatorInputDecodeError`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`Request facts do not match the selected calculator input schema.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`UnsupportedCalculatorError`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`The requested calculator id is not in the public catalogue.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`UnsupportedCalculatorContextError`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`The calculator exists, but not for the requested jurisdiction or tax year.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculationError`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`The calculation engine returned a source-backed domain failure.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculatorCapacityExceeded`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`The server has no free calculation place. Retry manually after the current work finishes.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculatorOperationTimedOut`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`The operation reached its time limit. Retry manually.`},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculatorRateLimited`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"The native per-client calculation limit was reached. Wait for `Retry-After` and retry manually.\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:\"`CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable`\"},{heading:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`The native request identity or rate limiter is unavailable. Retry manually.`},{heading:`owning-sources`,content:\"Calculator schemas: `packages/calculators/src/schemas.ts`\"},{heading:`owning-sources`,content:\"Calculator error projection: `packages/calculators/src/errors.ts`\"},{heading:`owning-sources`,content:\"SDK schema re-exports: `packages/sdk/typescript/src/schemas/index.ts`\"},{heading:`used-by`,content:`Type safety`},{heading:`used-by`,content:`API errors`},{heading:`used-by`,content:`Error reference`},{heading:`used-by`,content:`Examples`}],headings:[{id:`schema-reference`,content:`Schema reference`},{id:`calculatorrunrequest`,content:`CalculatorRunRequest`},{id:`calculatorrunresponse`,content:`CalculatorRunResponse`},{id:`calculatorserviceerror`,content:`CalculatorServiceError`},{id:`runtime-graph`,content:`Runtime graph`},{id:`owning-sources`,content:`Owning sources`},{id:`used-by`,content:`Used by`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#schema-reference`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Schema reference`})},{depth:2,url:`#calculatorrunrequest`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`CalculatorRunRequest`})},{depth:2,url:`#calculatorrunresponse`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`CalculatorRunResponse`})},{depth:2,url:`#calculatorserviceerror`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`CalculatorServiceError`})},{depth:2,url:`#runtime-graph`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Runtime graph`})},{depth:2,url:`#owning-sources`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Owning sources`})},{depth:2,url:`#used-by`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Used by`})}];function o(e){let n={a:`a`,code:`code`,h1:`h1`,h2:`h2`,li:`li`,p