n compact while still using the\nsame descriptor and schema contracts as the generic SDK facade.\n\n## Generic path [#generic-path]\n\n```ts\nimport { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nimport { TaxKit } from \"@taxkit/sdk\";\nimport { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\n\nconst report = await TaxKit.calculate(au.calculations.annualIncomeTax, {\n  taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\n});\n```\n\n## Advanced Effect path [#advanced-effect-path]\n\nUse the Effect SDK when you want to provide `PublicCalculatorService` through\nyour own Effect layer or when an in-process transport needs the full\n`CalculatorRunResponse`.\n\n```ts\nimport { calculateRunRequest } from \"@taxkit/sdk/effect\";\n```\n\n## Next steps [#next-steps]\n\n* Read [Plain SDK](/sdk/plain-sdk) for Promise-based usage.\n* Read [Safe SDK](/sdk/safe-sdk) for typed success and failure results.\n* Read [Effect SDK](/sdk/effect-sdk) for service composition.\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"                                    |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@taxkit/sdk`         | You want `TaxKit.calculate`, `TaxKit.safe.calculate` or `TaxKit.createClient`.                              |\n| `@taxkit/sdk/au`      | You want Australian calculator helpers and descriptors.                                                     |\n| `@taxkit/sdk/effect`  | You want `calculateRunRequest`, `calculateReportRequest`, `calculateReport` or Effect service requirements. |\n| `@taxkit/sdk/schemas` | You want `CalculatorRunRequest`, `CalculatorRunResponse`, `CalculatorServiceError` and SDK result schemas.  |\n\n## Beginner path [#beginner-path]\n\n```ts\nimport { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nimport { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\n\nconst report = await au.incomeTax.annual({\n  taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\n});\n```\n\nAustralian helpers keep the first calculation compact while still using the\nsame descriptor and schema contracts as the generic SDK facade.\n\n## Generic path [#generic-path]\n\n```ts\nimport { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nimport { TaxKit } from \"@taxkit/sdk\";\nimport { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\n\nconst report = await TaxKit.calculate(au.calculations.annualIncomeTax, {\n  taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\n});\n```\n\n## Advanced Effect path [#advanced-effect-path]\n\nUse the Effect SDK when you want to provide `PublicCalculatorService` through\nyour own Effect layer or when an in-process transport needs the full\n`CalculatorRunResponse`.\n\n```ts\nimport { calculateRunRequest } from \"@taxkit/sdk/effect\";\n```\n\n## Next steps [#next-steps]\n\n* Read [Plain SDK](/sdk/plain-sdk) for Promise-based usage.\n* Read [Safe SDK](/sdk/safe-sdk) for typed success and failure results.\n* Read [Effect SDK](/sdk/effect-sdk) for service composition.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7875},"formatted_output":"                                    |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `@taxkit/sdk`         | You want `TaxKit.calculate`, `TaxKit.safe.calculate` or `TaxKit.createClient`.                              |\n| `@taxkit/sdk/au`      | You want Australian calculator helpers and descriptors.                                                     |\n| `@taxkit/sdk/effect`  | You want `calculateRunRequest`, `calculateReportRequest`, `calculateReport` or Effect service requirements. |\n| `@taxkit/sdk/schemas` | You want `CalculatorRunRequest`, `CalculatorRunResponse`, `CalculatorServiceError` and SDK result schemas.  |\n\n## Beginner path [#beginner-path]\n\n```ts\nimport { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nimport { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\n\nconst report = await au.incomeTax.annual({\n  taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\n});\n```\n\nAustralian hel