er-safe exports such as\n  `@taxkit/docs-content/client` and `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs/render`.\n- Keep content service acquisition, live Layer composition and Effect runtime\n  execution in app-owned `.server.ts` modules. Run the focused import-boundary\n  audit and do not add a browser docs runtime.\n- Keep docs loader outcomes encoded until a direct route-root consumer restores\n  them through the browser-safe route boundary.\n- Use TanStack router links for internal docs routes so client navigation runs\n  the route loader. Preserve query and fragment semantics; keep ordinary\n  anchors for external, mail, download, repository-source and same-document\n  destinations.\n- Keep the skip link, one main landmark, labelled navigation, current-page\n  semantics, focus intent and responsive disclosure app-owned. Client\n  navigation may move focus to the page heading; initial hydration must not.\n- Keep all information and focus behavior available without animation. A\n  reduced-motion browser setting must not remove required state.\n- Do not import generated `.source/server` files or\n  `@taxkit/docs-content/server` from browser modules.\n- Keep Fumadocs generated source access inside `@taxkit/docs-content` server\n  values from the `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs/service` boundary.\n- Apply the [abstraction admission\n  contract](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md) before sharing a hook,\n  provider, component family or UI package.\n\n## Related Docs\n\n- [API and SDK](./api-and-sdk.md)\n- [Package ownership](./package-ownership.md)\n- [Content and posts](./content-and-posts.md)\n\nThe Website settings function takes no data or client Context. Its build-owned\nroute base and Worker ingress share `WebsiteServerFunctionBase`; query payloads\nand non-GET methods are rejected before TanStack's parser. Expected settings\nerrors remain encoded checked results. Unexpected settings failures use native\nHTTP matching/reporting and a native Response, bypassing error serialisation.\nThe saved native suite also qualifies controlled fatal/RPC paths and caller\ncancellation. T003's bounded local connection acceptance is complete; T009\nretains the unqualified safe trace exports.\n\nNative settings ingress admits the function's own generated URL, without\ncopying its build ID. Unknown IDs, extra path parts and missing IDs get empty\n404 responses before TanStack lookup; its native lookup otherwise logs unknown\nIDs even when the response body hides them.\n\nThe answer container uses native `AsyncResult.value` to retain the last success\nthrough refresh, failure and interruption. Submit does not reset that history.\nA checked server-submitted answer supplies the fallback before the first browser\nsuccess. The readonly leaf renders a named semantic `output` with an atomic\npolite announcement for both answer and out-of-date state. This state stays in\n\nThe docs app's focused server tests construct one ManagedRuntime with an\ninjected deterministic probe identity, read both the content and probe services\nconcurrently, prove stable construction state across reads, and dispose the\nruntime. The built workerd journey separately proves one emitted runtime/probe\nLayer, stable opt-in proof headers across initial, missing and concurrent\nrequests, SSR, hydration, client navigation, server functions, 404s and clean\nbrowser diagnostics. `test:cloudflare-built -- --screenshots` additionally\nwrites ignored desktop/mobile PNGs and a digest manifest for visual review.\nThose images supplement, but cannot replace, the behavioral oracles or prove\nprovider-global isolate lifetime.\n\nThe six current consumer-visible journeys, including the native Website, are maintained in\n[`../verification/critical-journeys.json`](../verification/critical-journeys.json):\ncalculator direct use, packed SDK, HTTP API, docs runtime, release closure and\nthe native Website. The original five-journey packet remains bounded, sanitised\nhistorical local evidence in\n[`../evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](../evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json);\nraw logs and transient tarballs are not committed. Complete sanitized command\ndetail is retained at unique ignored paths with digests, while a bounded attempt\nreceipt binds the verified base commit and changed-content manifest digest.\n`release:present` verifies that receipt and all referenced detail before writing\nor reusing an immutable presentation sidecar, so terminal output remains\nreconstructable without rerunning. The failed-provenance index retains prior\nterminal evidence outside the default route. Local browser proof does not prove deployed SSR,\nhydration or public availability, and no local receipt proves publication or\ndeployment.\n\nCandidate evidence verifies every sorted safe path and digest in its exact\nchanged-content manifest, plus the complete transient attempt receipt/detail\nchain. Accepted lifecycle evidence retains only the bounded sanitized JSON\nsummary in Git and does not require ignored raw command logs in a clean clone.\nA later release attempt must first prepare a new candidate packet; the runtime\nfails closed instead of reusing an accepted candidate identity. It compares the\nbase commit, manifest path and manifest digest with the accepted summary, so\nchanging lifecycle back to `candidate` alone cannot reuse an accepted proof.\n\n## Review evidence\n\nSubstantial code, package-boundary, API, SDK, app-runtime or documentation\nrollouts record the review evidence their changed boundaries require. Acceptance\nis based on path-evidenced task gates and semantic review, not a fixed number of\naudit passes or workers. Review the final code and command graphs against their\nowning architecture and SPEC; inspect Effect flow, schemas, tagged errors,\nunsafe casts, DTO mirrors, and helper or abstraction sprawl; then inspect the\nCI, lint, packed-consumer, browser/API, documentation, and Changeset evidence\nthat applies to the changed surface.\n\nNew shared abstractions must satisfy the\n[abstraction admission contract](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md).\nFocused tests must prove the claimed policy or substitution point; coverage\nthat only calls through a wrapper is not admission evidence. Static lint is a\nsupporting gate and cannot replace semantic ownership or call-graph review.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- A rule pack is incomplete without source references and golden tests.\n- Graph validation failures should fail the build.\n- API responses must stay schema-backed.\n- Public docs content must validate through `@taxkit/docs-content` before\n  documentation/runtime slices are accepted.\n- Keep browser tooling in app dev dependencies and browser harness routes out\n  of production route trees.\n- Browser-safe exports must not import Node-only modules.\n- Oxlint can enforce restricted APIs, such as banned `Object.*` enumeration\n  helpers, but it does not currently provide a safe built-in rule for banning\n  functions below a minimum line count. Prefer review and architecture guidance\n  for tiny one-off wrapper or mapper helpers.\n- `tools/oxlint/effect-rules.ts`, `bun-rules.ts` and `mdx-rules.ts` own\n  domain-neutral contracts. `taxkit-rules.ts` owns tax/calculator policy plus\n  decoder and route-transport rules. Do not put package names or tax defaults\n  into a portable rule message.\n- `tools/oxlint/anti-slop/**` is a separately installed generic rule owner.\n  `oxlint.config.ts` registers its generic and Effect plugins, enables every\n  admitted rule at error severity and keeps the vendored source under an exact\n  ignore. Do not copy its rules into TaxKit plugins or add broad source\n  exemptions to pass them.\n- Portable Effect rules ban manual `_tag` literals and `switch`, keep live/test\n  Layers out of service contracts, restrict encoder execution, reject throwing\n  Schema sync codecs, preserve typed service errors and tagged-error causes,\n  and keep runtime, console, process and host imports at configured boundaries.\nEffect-native subpaths, jurisdiction modules, examples, compatibility tests and\npacked-artifact checks. Its strict downstream validator may orchestrate the\nnine-package release closure and materialize package-declared publication\nexports in temporary tarballs, but package manifests and exports remain owned\nby their packages. It must not depend on `@taxkit/api-http`; HTTP\ntransports call the calculator service directly; the SDK is a test-only\ncomparison dependency of the HTTP package. Its Effect entrypoint owns\nrequest-preserving calculator helpers such as `calculateRunRequest`,\n`calculateReportRequest` and `calculateReport`, while reusing\ncalculator-owned `CalculatorRun*` schemas and `CalculatorServiceError`.\n\n`apps/web`\n: Native TanStack Website candidate. It owns form presentation/commands, the\n  server runner and React Atom registry. The private server binding and checked\n  public browser address reach the separate API through native RPC. The root\n  restores encoded outcomes. Tax rules and calculations remain package/API-owned;\n  full T003 acceptance and the other calculator pages remain in progress.\n\n`apps/docs`\n: Implemented public documentation app. It owns TanStack Start routes, the\n  docs app shell, route loaders, navigation presentation and app-local\n  MDX component composition, Schema-decoded build target, Cloudflare Vite\n  configuration, static-asset headers and local built-Worker proof. It\n  consumes package-owned content and Fumadocs helpers, but does not own\n  canonical frontmatter, navigation, generated source or reusable Fumadocs\n  integration contracts. It composes and executes one module-scoped\n  server-only managed runtime; browser code restores encoded route transport\n  and does not own an Effect runtime.\n\nRoot `alchemy.run.ts`\n: Repository deployment composition for the docs app. It owns Cloudflare\n  providers and remote state, decodes the stage, and calls the private\n"},"started_at_ms":1791301956433,"completed_at_ms":1791301956433}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T15:52:36.457Z","ordinal":48010,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-32afa674-7de0-4895-937f-312d96cfc801","process_id":"28583","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 6 'CSF-T005|data-free|server function|server-function|Q9|settings GET' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json'))\nprint(type(p))\nprint(json.dumps(p,indent=2)[0:2000])\nfor k,v in p.items():\n if isinstance(v,list):\n  for x in v:\n   if 'T005' in json.dumps(x):print(json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -C 6 'CSF-T005|data-free|server function|server-function|Q9|settings GET' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json'))\nprint(type(p))\nprint(json.dumps(p,indent=2)[0:2000])\nfor k,v in p.items():\n if isinstance(v,list):\n  for x in v:\n   if 'T005' in json.dumps(x):print(json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"112-telemetry tests -> checked event policy -> fake SDK/exporter -> no tax values\n113-controlled Preview journeys -> exact Website/API artifacts -> independent readback\n114-```\n115-\n116-## Interview decision tree\n117-\n118:### Website connection agreed in Q9\n119-\n120-Use native Effect RPC for named website operations. The proposed first\n121-transport is ordinary HTTP POST with the native JSON codec and Schema-derived\n122-success/error values. Existing calculators return one bounded result; they do\n123-not need WebSockets, persistent RPC sessions or an invented progress stream.\n124-Explicitly select `RpcServer.layerHttp({ protocol: \"http\", ... })` and\n--\n140-loader. Both implement the same named checked client contract and keep the\n141-native generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\n142-source loader, RPC server or backend fallback. Calculator facts go only in\n143-bounded bodies; reports live only in the current calculation/page state.\n144-Credentials are omitted and unexpected redirects rejected for public browser\n145-calls. Actual native request headers determine the tested CORS allowlist.\n146:The Website's native settings server function is a GET with no data or client\n147-Context. Its explicit build/ingress route uses the native generated function\n148-URL and rejects unknown or extended addresses with empty 404 before native\n149-lookup/logging. It rejects query payloads and unsupported methods before parsing; calculations remain body-only form/RPC requests.\n150-Expected settings errors keep their checked result. Unexpected settings failures\n151-use the native HTTP failure matcher and safe host reporter, then return the\n152-native empty response before TanStack can log or serialise an arbitrary error.\n--\n187-with handwritten framing or broadly convert every defect to an expected error.\n188-\n189-Sources: [selected native RPC server](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts),\n190-[client](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcClient.ts)\n191-and [serialisation](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcSerialization.ts).\n192-\n193:Q9 selects backend calculation through native RPC. Inputs are temporarily sent\n194-in bounded bodies, with no persisted figures or logged reports. Keep the rules\n195-out of the website bundle and provide no browser engine fallback. Protocol\n196-compatibility, error privacy and actual cancellation still need the named\n197-implementation checks; selecting the design does not prove them.\n198-\n199-### Settled interview choices\n--\n206-| Calculation privacy | Agreed in Q4: temporary only | No saved calculations, tax figures in URLs, calculation logs or personalised share images | Browser state lifetime and safe operational logging |\n207-| Browser agent actions | Agreed in Q5: allow all proposed actions | Find, fill, calculate and read; keep changes visible to the person | Tool scopes, cancellation and page state |\n208-| Documentation launch | Agreed in Q6: review and publish finished pages | Update and review pages; publish accepted pages and keep unfinished drafts out of public search | Publication records, search, sitemap, Markdown and agent indexes |\n209-| Public website and API addresses | Agreed in Q7: taxkit.dev, API subdomain and Alchemy-managed DNS/domain | Use taxkit.dev and api.taxkit.dev; follow the Common Practice ownership pattern | Canonical links, origins, sitemap, DNS and deployment routing |\n210-| Measurement | Agreed in Q8 and expanded by Cooper's latest message | PostHog visits and calculator names; Axiom logs, traces and metrics in the existing shared datasets; no calculation details or consent dialog | Event ownership, privacy checks, identity filters and retained provider resources |\n211-| Functional Effect policy | Required by Cooper's follow-up | Immutable values, declarative workflows, services/Layers and piping across all owned code; current portable rules plus proved corrections for remaining gaps | Mutation/loop restrictions, state ownership and precise host exceptions |\n212:| Website connection | Agreed in Q9 | Native Effect RPC to the same-stage backend; temporarily send calculation facts in a body | RPC contract/version, server binding/browser URL, failure and cancellation proof |\n213-| Calculation trigger | Agreed in Q10 | Explicit Calculate action; edits invalidate the old answer and interrupt old work | Form/result state and one usage event per successful action |\n214-| Result explanation | Agreed in Q11 | Main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and rule sources | Accessible result layout and checked explanation representations |\n215-| Homepage priority | Agreed in Q12 | Calculator-first homepage with clear developer/agent routes | Navigation and public landing pages |\n216-| Markdown scope | Agreed in Q13 | Accepted public docs and calculator reference pages only | Discovery/content representations; no personal report downloads in this release |\n217-\n218-Q1–Q13 are settled. The broader analytics request supersedes the earlier\n219-technical-health-only Q8 recommendation. Existing supported tax years stay\n220-explicit; unsupported years fail rather than silently falling back to another\n221-year. Share images describe public pages and never a person's figures. The 4 October implementation request admits the settled design.\n222:Cooper reopened the interview and has now accepted Q9–Q13. There are no further\n223-unresolved product branches in this first-release design. The 4 October implementation request supersedes the former Q14\n224-whole-design confirmation hold. The\n225-stronger functional Effect requirement is already explicit user direction,\n226-not another permission question.\n227-\n228-## Outcome, ownership and scope\n<class 'dict'>\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://taxkit.local/schemas/product-spec-task-plan.v1.json\",\n  \"spec\": \"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation \\u2014 implementation slices\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"last_reviewed\": \"2026-10-07\",\n  \"authority\": \"Cooper explicitly authorised implementation, reviewable commits and draft PRs on 2026-10-04. No merge, deploy or publication; provider-plan approval remains separate.\",\n  \"principles\": [\n    \"Retain tax rules/results and their proof while replacing application foundations.\",\n    \"Use immutable Schema-derived values and declarative, pipe-first Effect workflows across all owned apps/packages/tests/scripts/infrastructure; no local mutation, imperative loops or helper sprawl. Necessary state has a scoped React/Effect owner and pure updates.\",\n    \"One primary owner integrates and accepts whole slices; agent or test counts do not establish proof.\",\n    \"Every required owning document, README, rule, export, generated source, skill and runbook changes within the affected slice.\",\n    \"Use current qualified exact dependencies; no silent downgrade, broad exception or unproved peer override.\",\n    \"Each task is pending until its actual postconditions and applicable checks pass. Proposed tasks do not authorise cloud changes.\"\n  ],\n  \"globalVerification\": {\n    \"commitPolicy\": \"Commit coherent passed slices and prepare draft PRs under the 2026-10-04 implementation request. Do not merge, version-release, publish or deploy.\",\n    \"requiredBeforeFinalPR\": [\n      \"bun run verification\",\n      \"bun run test\",\n      \"bun run build\",\n      \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n      \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n      \"bun run release:check\",\n      \"bun run changeset:status\",\n      \"git diff --check\"\n    ],\n    \"evidenceRequired\": [\n      \"Final current/target/test call graph and exact candidate/version/configuration identity.\",\n      \"Actual-command rejection/acceptance fixtures for the complete 0.6\n{\n  \"surface\": \"App lifetimes and frontend/agents/content\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"apps/api/**\",\n    \"apps/web/**\",\n    \"apps/docs/**\",\n    \"packages/docs-content/**\",\n    \"packages/docs-fumadocs/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Version/tooling/lint/skills/CI and exact exports\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"package.json\",\n    \"bun.lock\",\n    \"turbo.json\",\n    \"oxlint.config.ts\",\n    \"oxfmt.config.ts\",\n    \"tsconfig*\",\n    \"knip*.json\",\n    \"tools/oxlint/**\",\n    \"tools/skills/**\",\n    \".agents/skills/**\",\n    \"AGENTS.md\",\n    \".github/workflows/**\",\n    \"tools/quality-workflow/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T007\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Semantic documentation, READMEs, generated/public status, runbooks and journeys\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"docs/README.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/**\",\n    \"docs/standards/**\",\n    \"docs/runbooks/**\",\n    \"docs/operations/authority-model.md\",\n    \"docs/verification/critical-journeys.json\",\n    \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json\",\n    \"tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n    \"Affected app/package README.md\",\n    \"docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T001\",\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\",\n    \"CSF-T007\",\n    \"CSF-T008\",\n    \"CSF-T009\",\n    \"CSF-T010\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Package versioning and consumer/release proof\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \".changeset/config.json\",\n    \".changeset/*.md\",\n    \"packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/**\",\n    \"packages/sdk/typescript/scripts/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T010\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n  \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-006\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n    \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n    \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n    \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n    \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n    \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n    \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n    \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n    \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n    \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n    \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n    \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n    \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run docs:validate\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n    \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n    \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n    \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n    \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n    \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-compiled-content-contract.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-native-docs-catalogue-source.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-page-copy-review.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-docs-links.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-acceptance.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-http.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-native-docs-connection.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T006\",\n  \"title\": \"Add remote MCP and visible browser agent tools\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-005\",\n    \"CSF-006\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Add native Effect remote MCP for catalogue/docs discovery, checked calculator inputs, execution and results, reusing the same named operations and accepted Markdown.\",\n    \"Select and qualify native Effect v2026_07_28 stateless and v2025_11_25 stateful adapters before advertising them. Apply anonymous request limits, allowed origins, bounded request/stream lifetimes, cancellation, typed errors and safe tool descriptions; publish discovery and setup docs.\",\n    \"Register feature-detected page-owned WebMCP tools for find/read/fill/calculate/read-result. Reuse visible website commands and the checked RPC client; unregister/cancel on route change or unmount. Do not add direct SDK/backend calls or a duplicate calculation/event owner.\",\n    \"Document actual browser support and distinguish protocol/schema registration from a real agent journey; ordinary browser use must keep working.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/api native MCP adapter and justified contract exports at the existing package owners\",\n    \"apps/web page-owned WebMCP registration/command owner and cleanup tests\",\n    \"Public agent setup/Markdown docs, app/package READMEs, owning architecture and critical-journey updates\",\n    \"HTTP/MCP/WebMCP equality, origin/rate/cancellation and browser evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\",\n    \"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\",\n    \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n    \"Remote and browser tools have actual caller evidence; lack of a supported browser is recorded as a proof gap, never a passed agent journey.\",\n    \"Anonymous access has bounded work and no required account or stored calculation.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T007\",\n  \"title\": \"Prepare DNS, domain and secret provider plans\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-007\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T005\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Read actual taxkit.dev zone/account, records, domain/registrar and DNSSEC state; classify existing state and preserve unrelated mail/verification records.\",\n    \"Declare adopted retained Production zone/settings and native taxkit.dev Website plus www redirect and api.taxkit.dev backend domain attachments; keep Preview away from Production DNS. Derive each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, with application-ingress Schema checks and checked failure for absent Outputs. Qualify local, Preview and custom-domain behaviour; domains are infrastructure inputs, not duplicated application-origin configuration.\",\n    \"Complete native Doppler stage selection, shell-source policy, named runtime bindings and distinct deploy/query/Turbo credentials; remove stale --env-file wrappers only with equivalent behaviour.\",\n    \"Produce version-matched no-apply plans and authority/rollback/readback procedures. Replace graph validators/workflow projection assumptions that admit only one DocsWebsite without adding a bespoke parallel deployment framework.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"packages/infrastructure native zone/domain/stage/secrets graph and root alchemy entries\",\n    \"tools/docs-deployment/** owning admission/secret/workflow replacements, relevant workflows and Turbo inputs\",\n    \"docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md, recovery.md, operations/authority-model.md and tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n    \"Redacted exact-resource plans, retention and DNS/secret readback procedures\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment:types\",\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment-tools:types\",\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment\",\n    \"bun run test:docs-deployment\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run check:repository-paths\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n    \"Doppler precedence, runtime binding and separate credential purposes have checked proof without secret values in output.\",\n    \"All cloud mutations remain unexecuted until the concrete plan has the required named authority; DNS/TLS/registrar readback is separate from apply success.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T008\",\n  \"title\": \"Implement minimal PostHog traffic and calculator analytics\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-008\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n    \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n    \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n    \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n    \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n    \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n    \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Inspect actual latest-SDK batches for only accepted page/calculator properties, no amounts/results/queries and no extra SDK endpoints.\",\n    \"Prove initial/client navigation counts including A-to-B-to-A, one successful-use event per action across UI/WebMCP/API/MCP, no event on failure/cancellation, and backend browser opt-out.\",\n    \"Check denied storage, DNT before/after acquisition, ordinary Preview/development off, cleanup and relay size/deadline/status/redirect failures.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n    \"One backend owner emits each successful hosted calculator use; pure packages/local SDK calculations send no analytics.\",\n    \"An event delivery response is transport proof only; exact provider UUID readback remains a separately authorised Preview journey.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"112-telemetry tests -> checked event policy -> fake SDK/exporter -> no tax values\n113-controlled Preview journeys -> exact Website/API artifacts -> independent readback\n114-```\n115-\n116-## Interview decision tree\n117-\n118:### Website connection agreed in Q9\n119-\n120-Use native Effect RPC for named website operations. The proposed first\n121-transport is ordinary HTTP POST with the native JSON codec and Schema-derived\n122-success/error values. Existing calculators return one bounded result; they do\n123-not need WebSockets, persistent RPC sessions or an invented progress stream.\n124-Explicitly select `RpcServer.layerHttp({ protocol: \"http\", ... })` and\n--\n140-loader. Both implement the same named checked client contract and keep the\n141-native generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\n142-source loader, RPC server or backend fallback. Calculator facts go only in\n143-bounded bodies; reports live only in the current calculation/page state.\n144-Credentials are omitted and unexpected redirects rejected for public browser\n145-calls. Actual native request headers determine the tested CORS allowlist.\n146:The Website's native settings server function is a GET with no data or client\n147-Context. Its explicit build/ingress route uses the native generated function\n148-URL and rejects unknown or extended addresses with empty 404 before native\n149-lookup/logging. It rejects query payloads and unsupported methods before parsing; calculations remain body-only form/RPC requests.\n150-Expected settings errors keep their checked result. Unexpected settings failures\n151-use the native HTTP failure matcher and safe host reporter, then return the\n152-native empty response before TanStack can log or serialise an arbitrary error.\n--\n187-with handwritten framing or broadly convert every defect to an expected error.\n188-\n189-Sources: [selected native RPC server](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts),\n190-[client](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcClient.ts)\n191-and [serialisation](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcSerialization.ts).\n192-\n193:Q9 selects backend calculation through native RPC. Inputs are temporarily sent\n194-in bounded bodies, with no persisted figures or logged reports. Keep the rules\n195-out of the website bundle and provide no browser engine fallback. Protocol\n196-compatibility, error privacy and actual cancellation still need the named\n197-implementation checks; selecting the design does not prove them.\n198-\n199-### Settled interview choices\n--\n206-| Calculation privacy | Agreed in Q4: temporary only | No saved calculations, tax figures in URLs, calculation logs or personalised share images | Browser state lifetime and safe operational logging |\n207-| Browser agent actions | Agreed in Q5: allow all proposed actions | Find, fill, calculate and read; keep changes visible to the person | Tool scopes, cancellation and page state |\n208-| Documentation launch | Agreed in Q6: review and publish finished pages | Update and review pages; publish accepted pages and keep unfinished drafts out of public search | Publication records, search, sitemap, Markdown and agent indexes |\n209-| Public website and API addresses | Agreed in Q7: taxkit.dev, API subdomain and Alchemy-managed DNS/domain | Use taxkit.dev and api.taxkit.dev; follow the Common Practice ownership pattern | Canonical links, origins, sitemap, DNS and deployment routing |\n210-| Measurement | Agreed in Q8 and expanded by Cooper's latest message | PostHog visits and calculator names; Axiom logs, traces and metrics in the existing shared datasets; no calculation details or consent dialog | Event ownership, privacy checks, identity filters and retained provider resources |\n211-| Functional Effect policy | Required by Cooper's follow-up | Immutable values, declarative workflows, services/Layers and piping across all owned code; current portable rules plus proved corrections for remaining gaps | Mutation/loop restrictions, state ownership and precise host exceptions |\n212:| Website connection | Agreed in Q9 | Native Effect RPC to the same-stage backend; temporarily send calculation facts in a body | RPC contract/version, server binding/browser URL, failure and cancellation proof |\n213-| Calculation trigger | Agreed in Q10 | Explicit Calculate action; edits invalidate the old answer and interrupt old work | Form/result state and one usage event per successful action |\n214-| Result explanation | Agreed in Q11 | Main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and rule sources | Accessible result layout and checked explanation representations |\n215-| Homepage priority | Agreed in Q12 | Calculator-first homepage with clear developer/agent routes | Navigation and public landing pages |\n216-| Markdown scope | Agreed in Q13 | Accepted public docs and calculator reference pages only | Discovery/content representations; no personal report downloads in this release |\n217-\n218-Q1–Q13 are settled. The broader analytics request supersedes the earlier\n219-technical-health-only Q8 recommendation. Existing supported tax years stay\n220-explicit; unsupported years fail rather than silently falling back to another\n221-year. Share images describe public pages and never a person's figures. The 4 October implementation request admits the settled design.\n222:Cooper reopened the interview and has now accepted Q9–Q13. There are no further\n223-unresolved product branches in this first-release design. The 4 October implementation request supersedes the former Q14\n224-whole-design confirmation hold. The\n225-stronger functional Effect requirement is already explicit user direction,\n226-not another permission question.\n227-\n228-## Outcome, ownership and scope\n<class 'dict'>\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://taxkit.local/schemas/product-spec-task-plan.v1.json\",\n  \"spec\": \"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation \\u2014 implementation slices\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"last_reviewed\": \"2026-10-07\",\n  \"authority\": \"Cooper explicitly authorised implementation, reviewable commits and draft PRs on 2026-10-04. No merge, deploy or publication; provider-plan approval remains separate.\",\n  \"principles\": [\n    \"Retain tax rules/results and their proof while replacing application foundations.\",\n    \"Use immutable Schema-derived values and declarative, pipe-first Effect workflows across all owned apps/packages/tests/scripts/infrastructure; no local mutation, imperative loops or helper sprawl. Necessary state has a scoped React/Effect owner and pure updates.\",\n    \"One primary owner integrates and accepts whole slices; agent or test counts do not establish proof.\",\n    \"Every required owning document, README, rule, export, generated source, skill and runbook changes within the affected slice.\",\n    \"Use current qualified exact dependencies; no silent downgrade, broad exception or unproved peer override.\",\n    \"Each task is pending until its actual postconditions and applicable checks pass. Proposed tasks do not authorise cloud changes.\"\n  ],\n  \"globalVerification\": {\n    \"commitPolicy\": \"Commit coherent passed slices and prepare draft PRs under the 2026-10-04 implementation request. Do not merge, version-release, publish or deploy.\",\n    \"requiredBeforeFinalPR\": [\n      \"bun run verification\",\n      \"bun run test\",\n      \"bun run build\",\n      \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n      \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n      \"bun run release:check\",\n      \"bun run changeset:status\",\n      \"git diff --check\"\n    ],\n    \"evidenceRequired\": [\n      \"Final current/target/test call graph and exact candidate/version/configuration identity.\",\n      \"Actual-command rejection/acceptance fixtures for the complete 0.6\n{\n  \"surface\": \"App lifetimes and frontend/agents/content\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"apps/api/**\",\n    \"apps/web/**\",\n    \"apps/docs/**\",\n    \"packages/docs-content/**\",\n    \"packages/docs-fumadocs/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Version/tooling/lint/skills/CI and exact exports\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"package.json\",\n    \"bun.lock\",\n    \"turbo.json\",\n    \"oxlint.config.ts\",\n    \"oxfmt.config.ts\",\n    \"tsconfig*\",\n    \"knip*.json\",\n    \"tools/oxlint/**\",\n    \"tools/skills/**\",\n    \".agents/skills/**\",\n    \"AGENTS.md\",\n    \".github/workflows/**\",\n    \"tools/quality-workflow/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T007\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Semantic documentation, READMEs, generated/public status, runbooks and journeys\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"docs/README.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/**\",\n    \"docs/standards/**\",\n    \"docs/runbooks/**\",\n    \"docs/operations/authority-model.md\",\n    \"docs/verification/critical-journeys.json\",\n    \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json\",\n    \"tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n    \"Affected app/package README.md\",\n    \"docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T001\",\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\",\n    \"CSF-T007\",\n    \"CSF-T008\",\n    \"CSF-T009\",\n    \"CSF-T010\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Package versioning and consumer/release proof\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \".changeset/config.json\",\n    \".changeset/*.md\",\n    \"packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/**\",\n    \"packages/sdk/typescript/scripts/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T010\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n  \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-006\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n    \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n    \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n    \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n    \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n    \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n    \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n    \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n    \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n    \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n    \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n    \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n    \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run docs:validate\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n    \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n    \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n    \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n    \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n    \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-compiled-content-contract.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-native-docs-catalogue-source.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-page-copy-review.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-docs-links.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-acceptance.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-http.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-native-docs-connection.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T006\",\n  \"title\": \"Add remote MCP and visible browser agent tools\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-005\",\n    \"CSF-006\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Add native Effect remote MCP for catalogue/docs discovery, checked calculator inputs, execution and results, reusing the same named operations and accepted Markdown.\",\n    \"Select and qualify native Effect v2026_07_28 stateless and v2025_11_25 stateful adapters before advertising them. Apply anonymous request limits, allowed origins, bounded request/stream lifetimes, cancellation, typed errors and safe tool descriptions; publish discovery and setup docs.\",\n    \"Register feature-detected page-owned WebMCP tools for find/read/fill/calculate/read-result. Reuse visible website commands and the checked RPC client; unregister/cancel on route change or unmount. Do not add direct SDK/backend calls or a duplicate calculation/event owner.\",\n    \"Document actual browser support and distinguish protocol/schema registration from a real agent journey; ordinary browser use must keep working.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/api native MCP adapter and justified contract exports at the existing package owners\",\n    \"apps/web page-owned WebMCP registration/command owner and cleanup tests\",\n    \"Public agent setup/Markdown docs, app/package READMEs, owning architecture and critical-journey updates\",\n    \"HTTP/MCP/WebMCP equality, origin/rate/cancellation and browser evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\",\n    \"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\",\n    \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n    \"Remote and browser tools have actual caller evidence; lack of a supported browser is recorded as a proof gap, never a passed agent journey.\",\n    \"Anonymous access has bounded work and no required account or stored calculation.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T007\",\n  \"title\": \"Prepare DNS, domain and secret provider plans\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-007\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T005\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Read actual taxkit.dev zone/account, records, domain/registrar and DNSSEC state; classify existing state and preserve unrelated mail/verification records.\",\n    \"Declare adopted retained Production zone/settings and native taxkit.dev Website plus www redirect and api.taxkit.dev backend domain attachments; keep Preview away from Production DNS. Derive each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, with application-ingress Schema checks and checked failure for absent Outputs. Qualify local, Preview and custom-domain behaviour; domains are infrastructure inputs, not duplicated application-origin configuration.\",\n    \"Complete native Doppler stage selection, shell-source policy, named runtime bindings and distinct deploy/query/Turbo credentials; remove stale --env-file wrappers only with equivalent behaviour.\",\n    \"Produce version-matched no-apply plans and authority/rollback/readback procedures. Replace graph validators/workflow projection assumptions that admit only one DocsWebsite without adding a bespoke parallel deployment framework.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"packages/infrastructure native zone/domain/stage/secrets graph and root alchemy entries\",\n    \"tools/docs-deployment/** owning admission/secret/workflow replacements, relevant workflows and Turbo inputs\",\n    \"docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md, recovery.md, operations/authority-model.md and tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n    \"Redacted exact-resource plans, retention and DNS/secret readback procedures\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment:types\",\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment-tools:types\",\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment\",\n    \"bun run test:docs-deployment\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run check:repository-paths\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n    \"Doppler precedence, runtime binding and separate credential purposes have checked proof without secret values in output.\",\n    \"All cloud mutations remain unexecuted until the concrete plan has the required named authority; DNS/TLS/registrar readback is separate from apply success.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T008\",\n  \"title\": \"Implement minimal PostHog traffic and calculator analytics\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-008\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n    \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n    \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n    \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n    \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n    \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n    \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Inspect actual latest-SDK batches for only accepted page/calculator properties, no amounts/results/queries and no extra SDK endpoints.\",\n    \"Prove initial/client navigation counts including A-to-B-to-A, one successful-use event per action across UI/WebMCP/API/MCP, no event on failure/cancellation, and backend browser opt-out.\",\n    \"Check denied storage, DNT before/after acquisition, ordinary Preview/development off, cleanup and relay size/deadline/status/redirect failures.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n    \"One backend owner emits each successful hosted calculator use; pure packages/local SDK calculations send no analytics.\",\n    \"An event delivery response is transport proof only; exact provider UUID readback remains a separately authorised Preview journey.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6958},"formatted_output":"112-telemetry tests -> checked event policy -> fake SDK/exporter -> no tax values\n113-controlled Preview journeys -> exact Website/API artifacts -> independent readback\n114-```\n115-\n116-## Interview decision tree\n117-\n118:### Website connection agreed in Q9\n119-\n120-Use native Effect RPC for named website operations. The proposed first\n121-transport is ordinary HTTP POST with the native JSON codec and Schema-derived\n122-success/error values. Existing calculators return one bounded result; they do\n123-not need WebSockets, persistent RPC sessions or an invented progress stream.\n124-Explicitly select `RpcServer.layerHttp({ protocol: \"http\", ... })` and\n--\n140-loader. Both implement the same named checked client contract and keep the\n141-native generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\n142-source loader, RPC server or backend fallback. Calculator facts go only in\n143-bounded bodies; reports live only in the current calculation/page state.\n144-Credentials are omitted and unexpected redirects rejected for public browser\n145-calls. Actual native request headers determine the tested CORS allowlist.\n146:The Website's native settings server function is a GET with no data or client\n147-Context. Its explicit build/ingress route uses the native generated function\n148-URL and rejects unknown or extended addresses with empty 404 before native\n149-lookup/logging. It rejects query payloads and unsupported methods before parsing; calculations remain body-only form/RPC requests.\n150-Expected settings errors keep their checked result. Unexpected settings failures\n151-use the native HTTP failure matcher and safe host reporter, then return the\n152-native empty response before TanStack can log or serialise an arbitrary error.\n--\n187-with handwritten framing or broadly convert every defect to an expected error.\n188-\n189-Sources: [selected native RPC server](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts),\n190-[client](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcClient.ts)\n191-and [serialisation](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcSerialization.ts).\n192-\n193:Q9 selects backend calculation through native RPC. Inputs are temporarily sent\n194-in bounded bodies, with no persisted figures or logged reports. Keep the rules\n195-out of the website bundle and provide no browser engine fallback. Protocol\n196-compatibility, error privacy and actual cancellation still need the named\n197-implementation checks; selecting the design does not prove them.\n198-\n199-### Settled interview choices\n--\n206-| Calculation privacy | Agreed in Q4: temporary only | No saved calculations, tax figures in URLs, calculation logs or personalised share images | Browser state lifetime and safe operational logging |\n207-| Browser agent actions | Agreed in Q5: allow all proposed actions | Find, fill, calculate and read; keep changes visible to the person | Tool scopes, cancellation and page state |\n208-| Documentation launch | Agreed in Q6: review and publish finished pages | Update and review pages; publish accepted pages and keep unfinished drafts out of public search | Publication records, search, sitemap, Markdown and agent indexes |\n209-| Public website and API addresses | Agreed in Q7: taxkit.dev, API subdomain and Alchemy-managed DNS/domain | Use taxkit.dev and api.taxkit.dev; follow the Common Practice ownership pattern | Canonical links, origins, sitemap, DNS and deployment routing |\n210-| Measurement | Agreed in Q8 and expanded by Cooper's latest message | PostHog visits and calculator names; Axiom logs, traces and metrics in the existing shared datasets; no calculation details or consent dialog | Event ownership, privacy checks, identity filters and retained provider resources |\n211-| Functional Effect policy | Required by Cooper's follow-up | Immutable values, declarative workflows, services/Layers and piping across all owned code; current portable rules plus proved corrections for remaining gaps | Mutation/loop restrictions, state ownership and precise host exceptions |\n212:| Website connection | Agreed in Q9 | Native Effect RPC to the same-stage backend; temporarily send calculation facts in a body | RPC contract/version, server binding/browser URL, failure and cancellation proof |\n213-| Calculation trigger | Agreed in Q10 | Explicit Calculate action; edits invalidate the old answer and interrupt old work | Form/result state and one usage event per successful action |\n214-| Result explanation | Agreed in Q11 | Main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and rule sources | Accessible result layout and checked explanation representations |\n215-| Homepage priority | Agreed in Q12 | Calculator-first homepage with clear developer/agent routes | Navigation and public landing pages |\n216-| Markdown scope | Agreed in Q13 | Accepted public docs and calculator reference pages only | Discovery/content representations; no personal report downloads in this release |\n217-\n218-Q1–Q13 are settled. The broader analytics request supersedes the earlier\n219-technical-health-only Q8 recommendation. Existing supported tax years stay\n220-explicit; unsupported years fail rather than silently falling back to another\n221-year. Share images describe public pages and never a person's figures. The 4 October implementation request admits the settled design.\n222:Cooper reopened the interview and has now accepted Q9–Q13. There are no further\n223-unresolved product branches in this first-release design. The 4 October implementation request supersedes the former Q14\n224-whole-design confirmation hold. The\n225-stronger functional Effect requirement is already explicit user direction,\n226-not another permission question.\n227-\n228-## Outcome, ownership and scope\n<class 'dict'>\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://taxkit.local/schemas/product-spec-task-plan.v1.json\",\n  \"spec\": \"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Clean slate TaxKit foundation \\u2014 implementation slices\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"last_reviewed\": \"2026-10-07\",\n  \"authority\": \"Cooper explicitly authorised implementation, reviewable commits and draft PRs on 2026-10-04. No merge, deploy or publication; provider-plan approval remains separate.\",\n  \"principles\": [\n    \"Retain tax rules/results and their proof while replacing application foundations.\",\n    \"Use immutable Schema-derived values and declarative, pipe-first Effect workflows across all owned apps/packages/tests/scripts/infrastructure; no local mutation, imperative loops or helper sprawl. Necessary state has a scoped React/Effect owner and pure updates.\",\n    \"One primary owner integrates and accepts whole slices; agent or test counts do not establish proof.\",\n    \"Every required owning document, README, rule, export, generated source, skill and runbook changes within the affected slice.\",\n    \"Use current qualified exact dependencies; no silent downgrade, broad exception or unproved peer override.\",\n    \"Each task is pending until its actual postconditions and applicable checks pass. Proposed tasks do not authorise cloud changes.\"\n  ],\n  \"globalVerification\": {\n    \"commitPolicy\": \"Commit coherent passed slices and prepare draft PRs under the 2026-10-04 implementation request. Do not merge, version-release, publish or deploy.\",\n    \"requiredBeforeFinalPR\": [\n      \"bun run verification\",\n      \"bun run test\",\n      \"bun run build\",\n      \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n      \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n      \"bun run release:check\",\n      \"bun run changeset:status\",\n      \"git diff --check\"\n    ],\n    \"evidenceRequired\": [\n      \"Final current/target/test call graph and exact candidate/version/configuration identity.\",\n      \"Actual-command rejection/acceptance fixtures for the complete 0.6\n{\n  \"surface\": \"App lifetimes and frontend/agents/content\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"apps/api/**\",\n    \"apps/web/**\",\n    \"apps/docs/**\",\n    \"packages/docs-content/**\",\n    \"packages/docs-fumadocs/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Version/tooling/lint/skills/CI and exact exports\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"package.json\",\n    \"bun.lock\",\n    \"turbo.json\",\n    \"oxlint.config.ts\",\n    \"oxfmt.config.ts\",\n    \"tsconfig*\",\n    \"knip*.json\",\n    \"tools/oxlint/**\",\n    \"tools/skills/**\",\n    \".agents/skills/**\",\n    \"AGENTS.md\",\n    \".github/workflows/**\",\n    \"tools/quality-workflow/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T007\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Semantic documentation, READMEs, generated/public status, runbooks and journeys\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"docs/README.md\",\n    \"docs/architecture/**\",\n    \"docs/standards/**\",\n    \"docs/runbooks/**\",\n    \"docs/operations/authority-model.md\",\n    \"docs/verification/critical-journeys.json\",\n    \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json\",\n    \"tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n    \"Affected app/package README.md\",\n    \"docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T001\",\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\",\n    \"CSF-T007\",\n    \"CSF-T008\",\n    \"CSF-T009\",\n    \"CSF-T010\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"surface\": \"Package versioning and consumer/release proof\",\n  \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n  \"paths\": [\n    \".changeset/config.json\",\n    \".changeset/*.md\",\n    \"packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/**\",\n    \"packages/sdk/typescript/scripts/**\"\n  ],\n  \"tasks\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\",\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T010\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n  \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-006\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T004\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n    \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n    \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n    \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n    \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n    \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n    \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n    \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n    \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n    \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n    \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n    \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n    \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run docs:validate\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n    \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n    \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n    \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n    \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n    \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-compiled-content-contract.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-native-docs-catalogue-source.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-page-copy-review.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-docs-links.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-acceptance.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-http.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-native-docs-connection.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T006\",\n  \"title\": \"Add remote MCP and visible browser agent tools\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-005\",\n    \"CSF-006\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Add native Effect remote MCP for catalogue/docs discovery, checked calculator inputs, execution and results, reusing the same named operations and accepted Markdown.\",\n    \"Select and qualify native Effect v2026_07_28 stateless and v2025_11_25 stateful adapters before advertising them. Apply anonymous request limits, allowed origins, bounded request/stream lifetimes, cancellation, typed errors and safe tool descriptions; publish discovery and setup docs.\",\n    \"Register feature-detected page-owned WebMCP tools for find/read/fill/calculate/read-result. Reuse visible website commands and the checked RPC client; unregister/cancel on route change or unmount. Do not add direct SDK/backend calls or a duplicate calculation/event owner.\",\n    \"Document actual browser support and distinguish protocol/schema registration from a real agent journey; ordinary browser use must keep working.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/api native MCP adapter and justified contract exports at the existing package owners\",\n    \"apps/web page-owned WebMCP registration/command owner and cleanup tests\",\n    \"Public agent setup/Markdown docs, app/package READMEs, owning architecture and critical-journey updates\",\n    \"HTTP/MCP/WebMCP equality, origin/rate/cancellation and browser evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\",\n    \"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\",\n    \"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\",\n    \"Remote and browser tools have actual caller evidence; lack of a supported browser is recorded as a proof gap, never a passed agent journey.\",\n    \"Anonymous access has bounded work and no required account or stored calculation.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T007\",\n  \"title\": \"Prepare DNS, domain and secret provider plans\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-007\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\",\n    \"CSF-T005\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Read actual taxkit.dev zone/account, records, domain/registrar and DNSSEC state; classify existing state and preserve unrelated mail/verification records.\",\n    \"Declare adopted retained Production zone/settings and native taxkit.dev Website plus www redirect and api.taxkit.dev backend domain attachments; keep Preview away from Production DNS. Derive each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, with application-ingress Schema checks and checked failure for absent Outputs. Qualify local, Preview and custom-domain behaviour; domains are infrastructure inputs, not duplicated application-origin configuration.\",\n    \"Complete native Doppler stage selection, shell-source policy, named runtime bindings and distinct deploy/query/Turbo credentials; remove stale --env-file wrappers only with equivalent behaviour.\",\n    \"Produce version-matched no-apply plans and authority/rollback/readback procedures. Replace graph validators/workflow projection assumptions that admit only one DocsWebsite without adding a bespoke parallel deployment framework.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"packages/infrastructure native zone/domain/stage/secrets graph and root alchemy entries\",\n    \"tools/docs-deployment/** owning admission/secret/workflow replacements, relevant workflows and Turbo inputs\",\n    \"docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md, recovery.md, operations/authority-model.md and tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\",\n    \"Redacted exact-resource plans, retention and DNS/secret readback procedures\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment:types\",\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment-tools:types\",\n    \"bun run check:docs-deployment\",\n    \"bun run test:docs-deployment\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run check:repository-paths\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\",\n    \"Doppler precedence, runtime binding and separate credential purposes have checked proof without secret values in output.\",\n    \"All cloud mutations remain unexecuted until the concrete plan has the required named authority; DNS/TLS/registrar readback is separate from apply success.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T008\",\n  \"title\": \"Implement minimal PostHog traffic and calculator analytics\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-008\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T004\",\n    \"CSF-T005\",\n    \"CSF-T006\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\",\n    \"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\",\n    \"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\",\n    \"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\",\n    \"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\",\n    \"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\",\n    \"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run check:docs\",\n    \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Inspect actual latest-SDK batches for only accepted page/calculator properties, no amounts/results/queries and no extra SDK endpoints.\",\n    \"Prove initial/client navigation counts including A-to-B-to-A, one successful-use event per action across UI/WebMCP/API/MCP, no event on failure/cancellation, and backend browser opt-out.\",\n    \"Check denied storage, DNT before/after acquisition, ordinary Preview/development off, cleanup and relay size/deadline/status/redirect failures.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\",\n    \"One backend owner emits each successful hosted calculator use; pure packages/local SDK calculations send no analytics.\",\n    \"An event delivery response is transport proof only; exact provider UUID readback remains a separately authorised Preview journey.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791301956457,"completed_at_ms":1791301956457}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T15:52:36.512Z","ordinal":48011,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a111ea-b3a0-7392-9261-5febfa57efa5","call_id":"call_vA9BGRtGTNHb7jQNZMn5PKQ4","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 12334)\nTotal output lines: 3\n\n{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"87075f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005916,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3666,\"output\":\"```ts\\nDocsContentService Effect\\n  -> browser-safe Schema.Exit JSON encoding\\n    -> createServerFn and route loader return encoded data unchanged\\n      -> SSR hydration or client-navigation transport\\n        -> direct route-root restore\\n          -> Result match\\n            -> canonical values reach composition and leaves\\n```\\n\\n## Decoding and composition boundaries\\n\\nRoute loaders, actions and dedicated boundary adapters own executable decoding\\nof URL state, browser storage, external HTTP responses and other transport\\nrepresentations. Prefer extracting a focused boundary module when a TanStack\\nroute file also renders React; do not allowlist a mixed `.tsx` route merely\\nbecause its loader needs a decoder.\\n\\nFor encoded TanStack loader state, the browser-safe boundary adapter owns the\\nSchema decoder and exposes a synchronous restore operation. The direct route\\ncomponent or route-owned `head` callback may call that operation when it is the\\nfirst consumer of loader data. This is an explicit transport boundary, not a\\ngeneral render-time decoder exception. The consumer uses one immutable loader\\ndata binding, restores once per invocation and matches the resulting\\n`Result.Result<Success, ExpectedFailure | TransportFailure>` itself.\\n\\nRoute composition then uses `Result`, `Option` or `Match` over schema-derived\\nvalues. It must not forward the encoded value or whole route `Result` to a\\nchild, and it must not hide restoration in a hook, provider, higher-order\\ncomponent, callback or one-use wrapper.\\n\\nLeaf components receive focused readonly values, callbacks or `children` from\\ntheir typed container and render only. They may own local interaction state,\\nbut must not accept representation-level `unknown`, call a decoder, acquire an\\nEffect service, create or run a runtime, read storage or environment directly,\\nor fetch their own boundary data. Pass commands from the loader, action or\\nowning container instead.\\n\\n## Visible composition and leaf ownership\\n\\nKeep the visible composition route-high. The route root owns restoration and\\ntop-level outcome matching, then renders the page shell and major semantic\\nlandmarks such as `header`, `nav`, `main`, `aside` and `footer`. A section\\ncontainer may arrange one coherent feature, but it must not hide the page's\\nprimary hierarchy behind a generic provider, hook or wrapper. Use one `main`\\nlandmark per page and keep landmark labels and heading order meaningful when\\nsections are rendered independently.\\n\\nPlace loading, empty, unavailable and recoverable error UI at the smallest\\ncomposition boundary that owns the failed data. Preserve the surrounding shell\\nand unrelated landmarks. A constrained panel, table, chart or control keeps a\\nstable footprint while its fallback is shown so dynamic states do not shift or\\noverlap adjacent content. Use a route-wide fallback only when the route cannot\\nestablish the page composition at all.\\n\\nLeaf props are focused and `readonly`: pass the canonical scalar, value object,\\nsmall schema-derived view or callback the leaf renders, not a transport DTO,\\nwhole route result, service or broad page model. Leaves may own complete local\\nUI commands such as disclosure, focus, copy or dialog state. A command that\\ncrosses a trust boundary, mutates domain state or invokes a remote operation is\\nowned by the route action or nearest policy-owning container and reaches the\\nleaf as a focused callback. The leaf may bind that callback to an event; it\\nmust not construct another runtime, service or transport client to execute it.\\n\\n```ts\\nroute loader/action or server function\\n  -> direct route-root restore and Result match\\n    -> page shell and semantic landmarks\\n      -> section container and smallest owning fallback\\n        -> leaf with readonly values and focused commands\\n```\\n\\nDo not add a hook, provider or wrapper component only to relocate a decoder or\\nsilence lint. Extract React composition when it owns reusable UI policy or\\nremoves meaningful repetition. App-specific composition remains app-owned;\\nthe docs accessibility and navigation UI stays in `apps/docs`, and this slice\\ndoes not create or depend on `packages/ui`.\\n\\nMDX component registries follow the same composition rule. The docs app owns\\none registry under its MDX adapter, while routes and leaves import focused\\nrender primitives or the app-owned registry. `mdx/no-route-local-component-registry`\\nenforces route placement; it does not move the registry into a shared package\\nbefore a second application needs it.\\n\\n## Guardrails\\n\\n- Keep app state conversion outside the deterministic engine.\\n- Decode boundary inputs before invoking calculators and before React\\n  composition begins.\\n- Do not import server-only API exports from browser routes.\\n- Do not remount the canonical API inside TanStack Start.\\n- Keep frontend docs and component details out of rule packages.\\n- Keep browser docs modules on browser-safe exports such as\\n  `@taxkit/docs-content/client` and `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs/render`.\\n- Keep content service acquisition, live Layer composition and Effect runtime\\n  execution in app-owned `.server.ts` modules. Run the focused import-boundary\\n  audit and do not add a browser docs runtime.\\n- Keep docs loader outcomes encoded until a direct route-root consumer restores\\n  them through the browser-safe route boundary.\\n- Use TanStack router links for internal docs routes so client navigation runs\\n  the route loader. Preserve query and fragment semantics; keep ordinary\\n  anchors for external, mail, download, repository-source and same-document\\n  destinations.\\n- Keep the skip link, one main landmark, labelled navigation, current-page\\n  semantics, focus intent and responsive disclosure app-owned. Client\\n  navigation may move focus to the page heading; initial hydration must not.\\n- Keep all information and focus behavior available without animation. A\\n  reduced-motion browser setting must not remove required state.\\n- Do not import generated `.source/server` files or\\n  `@taxkit/docs-content/server` from browser modules.\\n- Keep Fumadocs generated source access inside `@taxkit/docs-content` server\\n  values from the `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs/service` boundary.\\n- Apply the [abstraction admission\\n  contract](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md) before sharing a hook,\\n  provider, component family or UI package.\\n\\n## Related Docs\\n\\n- [API and SDK](./api-and-sdk.md)\\n- [Package ownership](./package-ownership.md)\\n- [Content and posts](./content-and-posts.md)\\n\\nThe Website settings function takes no data or client Context. Its build-owned\\nroute base and Worker ingress share `WebsiteServerFunctionBase`; query payloads\\nand non-GET methods are rejected before TanStack's parser. Expected settings\\nerrors remain encoded checked results. Unexpected settings failures use native\\nHTTP matching/reporting and a native Response, bypassing error serialisation.\\nThe saved native suite also qualifies controlled fatal/RPC paths and caller\\ncancellation. T003's bounded local connection acceptance is complete; T009\\nretains the unqualified safe trace exports.\\n\\nNative settings ingress admits the function's own generated URL, without\\ncopying its build ID. Unknown IDs, extra path parts and missing IDs get empty\\n404 responses before TanStack lookup; its native lookup otherwise logs unknown\\nIDs even when the response body hides them.\\n\\nThe answer container uses native `AsyncResult.value` to retain the last success\\nthrough refresh, failure and interruption. Submit does not reset that history.\\nA checked server-submitted answer supplies the fallback before the first browser\\nsuccess. The readonly leaf renders a named semantic `output` with an atomic\\npolite announcement for both answer and out-of-date state. This state stays in\\n\\nThe docs app's focused server tests construct one ManagedRuntime with an\\ninjected deterministic probe identity, read both the content and probe services\\nconcurrently, prove stable construction state across reads, and dispose the\\nruntime. The built workerd journey separately proves one emitted runtime/probe\\nLayer, stable opt-in proof headers across initial, missing and concurrent\\nrequests, SSR, hydration, client navigation, server functions, 404s and clean\\nbrowser diagnostics. `test:cloudflare-built -- --screenshots` additionally\\nwrites ignored desktop/mobile PNGs and a digest manifest for visual review.\\nThose images supplement, but cannot replace, the behavioral oracles or prove\\nprovider-global isolate lifetime.\\n\\nThe six current consumer-visible journeys, including the native Website, are maintained in\\n[`../verification/critical-journeys.json`](../verification/critical-journeys.json):\\ncalculator direct use, packed SDK, HTTP API, docs runtime, release closure and\\nthe native Website. The original five-journey packet remains bounded, sanitised\\nhistorical local evidence in\\n[`../evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](../evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json);\\nraw logs and transient tarballs are not committed. Complete sanitized command\\ndetail is retained at unique ignored paths with digests, while a bounded attempt\\nreceipt binds the verified base commit and changed-content manifest digest.\\n`release:present` verifies that receipt and all referenced detail before writing\\nor reusing an immutable presentation sidecar, so terminal output remains\\nreconstructable without rerunning. The failed-provenance index retains prior\\nterminal evidence outside the default route. Local browser proof does not prove deployed SSR,\\nhydration or public availability, and no local receipt proves publication or\\ndeployment.\\n\\nCandidate evidence verifies every sorted safe path and digest in its exact\\nchanged-content manifest, plus the complete transient attempt receipt/detail\\nchain. Accepted lifecycle evidence retains only the bounded sanitized JSON\\nsummary in Git and does not require ignored raw command logs in a clean clone.\\nA later release attempt must first prepare a new candidate packet; the runtime\\nfails closed instead of reusing an accepted candidate identity. It compares the\\nbase commit, manifest path and manifest digest with the accepted summary, so\\nchanging lifecycle back to `candidate` alone cannot reuse an accepted proof.\\n\\n## Review evidence\\n\\nSubstantial code, package-boundary, API, SDK, app-runtime or documentation\\nrollouts record the review evidence their changed boundaries require. Acceptance\\nis based on path-evidenced task gates and semantic review, not a fixed number of\\naudit passes or workers. Review the final code and command graphs against their\\nowning architecture and SPEC; inspect Effect flow, schemas, tagged errors,\\nunsafe casts, DTO mirrors, and helper or abstraction sprawl; then inspect the\\nCI, lint, packed-consumer, browser/API, documentation, and Changeset evidence\\nthat applies to the changed surface.\\n\\nNew shared abstractions must satisfy the\\n[abstraction admission contract](../design-docs/abstraction-admission.md).\\nFocused tests must prove the claimed policy or substitution point; coverage\\nthat only calls through a wrapper is not admission evidence. Static lint is a\\nsupporting gate and cannot replace semantic ownership or call-graph review.\\n\\n## Guardrails\\n\\n- A rule pack is incomplete without source references and golden tests.\\n- Graph validation failures should fail the build.\\n- API responses must stay schema-backed.\\n- Public docs content must validate through `@taxkit/docs-content` before\\n  documentation/runtime slices are accepted.\\n- Keep browser tooling in app dev dependencies and browser harness routes out\\n  of production route trees.\\n- Browser-safe exports must not import Node-only modules.\\n- Oxlint can enforce restricted APIs, such as banned `Object.*` enumeration\\n  helpers, but it does not currently provide a safe built-in rule for banning\\n  functions below a minimum line count. Prefer review and architecture guidance\\n  for tiny one-off wrapper or mapper helpers.\\n- `tools/oxlint/effect-rules.ts`, `bun-rules.ts` and `mdx-rules.ts` own\\n  domain-neutral contracts. `taxkit-rules.ts` owns tax/calculator policy plus\\n  decoder and route-transport rules. Do not put package names or tax defaults\\n  into a portable rule message.\\n- `tools/oxlint/anti-slop/**` is a separately installed generic rule owner.\\n  `oxlint.config.ts` registers its generic and Effect plugins, enables every\\n  admitted rule at error severity and keeps the vendored source under an exact\\n  ignore. Do not copy its rules into TaxKit plugins or add broad source\\n  exemptions to pass them.\\n- Portable Effect rules ban manual `_tag` literals and `switch`, keep live/test\\n  Layers out of service contracts, restrict encoder execution, reject throwing\\n  Schema sync codecs, preserve typed service errors and tagged-error causes,\\n  and keep runtime, console, process and host imports at configured boundaries.\\nEffect-native subpaths, jurisdiction modules, examples, compatibility tests and\\npacked-artifact checks. Its strict downstream validator may orchestrate the\\nnine-package release closure and materialize package-declared publication\\nexports in temporary tarballs, but package manifests and exports remain owned\\nby their packages. It must not depend on `@taxkit/api-http`; HTTP\\ntransports call the calculator service directly; the SDK is a test-only\\ncomparison dependency of the HTTP package. Its Effect entrypoint owns\\nrequest-preserving calculator helpers such as `calculateRunRequest`,\\n`calculateReportRequest` and `calculateReport`, while reusing\\ncalculator-owned `CalculatorRun*` schemas and `CalculatorServiceError`.\\n\\n`apps/web`\\n: Native TanStack Website candidate. It owns form presentation/commands, the\\n  server runner and React Atom registry. The private server binding and checked\\n  public browser address reach the separate API through native RPC. The root\\n  restores encoded outcomes. Tax rules and calculations remain package/API-owned;\\n  full T003 acceptance and the other calculator pages remain in progress.\\n\\n`apps/docs`\\n: Implemented public documentation app. It owns TanStack Start routes, the\\n  docs app shell, route loaders, navigation presentation and app-local\\n  MDX component composition, Schema-decoded build target, Cloudflare Vite\\n  configuration, static-asset headers and local built-Worker proof. It\\n  consumes package-owned content and Fumadocs helpers, but does not own\\n  canonical frontmatter, navigation, generated source or reusable Fumadocs\\n  integration contracts. It composes and executes one module-scoped\\n  server-only managed runtime; browser code restores encoded route transport\\n  and does not own an Effect runtime.\\n\\nRoot `alchemy.run.ts`\\n: Repository deployment composition for the docs app. It owns Cloudflare\\n  providers and remote state, decodes the stage, and calls the private\\n\"}}\n{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"a5152a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006958,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":8157,\"output\":\"112-telemetry tests -> checked event policy -> fake SDK/exporter -> no tax values\\n113-controlled Preview journeys -> exact Website/API artifacts -> independent readback\\n114-```\\n115-\\n116-## Interview decision tree\\n117-\\n118:### Website connection agreed in Q9\\n119-\\n120-Use native Effect RPC for named website operations. The proposed first\\n121-transport is ordinary HTTP POST with the native JSON codec and Schema-derived\\n122-success/error values. Existing calculators return one bounded result; they do\\n123-not need WebSockets, persistent RPC sessions or an invented progress stream.\\n124-Explicitly select `RpcServer.layerHttp({ protocol: \\\"http\\\", ... })` and\\n--\\n140-loader. Both implement the same named checked client contract and keep the\\n141-native generated client private. The Website has no live rule engine, authored\\n142-source loader, RPC server or backend fallback. Calculator facts go only in\\n143-bounded bodies; reports live only in the current calculation/page state.\\n144-Credentials are omitted and unexpected redirects rejected for public browser\\n145-calls. Actual native request headers determine the tested CORS allowlist.\\n146:The Website's native settings server function is a GET with no data or client\\n147-Context. Its explicit build/ingress route uses the native generated function\\n148-URL and rejects unknown or extended addresses with empty 404 before native\\n149-lookup/logging. It rejects query payloads and unsupported methods before parsing; calculations remain body-only form/RPC requests.\\n150-Expected settings errors keep their checked result. Unexpected settings failures\\n151-use the native HTTP failure matcher and safe host reporter, then return the\\n152-native empty response before TanStack can log or serialise an arbitrary error.\\n--\\n187-with handwritten framing or broadly convert every defect to an expected error.\\n188-\\n189-Sources: [selected native RPC server](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts),\\n190-[client](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcClient.ts)\\n191-and [serialisation](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/rpc/RpcSerialization.ts).\\n192-\\n193:Q9 selects backend calculation through native RPC. Inputs are temporarily sent\\n194-in bounded bodies, with no persisted figures or logged reports. Keep the rules\\n195-out of the website bundle and provide no browser engine fallback. Protocol\\n196-compatibility, error privacy and actual cancellation still need the named\\n197-implementation checks; selecting the design does not prove them.\\n198-\\n199-### Settled interview choices\\n--\\n206-| Calculation privacy | Agreed in Q4: temporary only | No saved calculations, tax figures in URLs, calculation logs or personalised share images | Browser state lifetime and safe operational logging |\\n207-| Browser agent actions | Agreed in Q5: allow all proposed actions | Find, fill, calculate and read; keep changes visible to the person | Tool scopes, cancellation and page state |\\n208-| Documentation launch | Agreed in Q6: review and publish finished pages | Update and review pages; publish accepted pages and keep unfinished drafts out of public search | Publication records, search, sitemap, Markdown and agent indexes |\\n209-| Public website and API addresses | Agreed in Q7: taxkit.dev, API subdomain and Alchemy-managed DNS/domain | Use taxkit.dev and api.taxkit.dev; follow the Common Practice ownership pattern | Canonical links, origins, sitemap, DNS and deployment routing |\\n210-| Measurement | Agreed in Q8 and expanded by Cooper's latest message | PostHog visits and calculator names; Axiom logs, traces and metrics in the existing shared datasets; no calculation details or consent dialog | Event ownership, privacy checks, identity filters and retained provider resources |\\n211-| Functional Effect policy | Required by Cooper's follow-up | Immutable values, declarative workflows, services/Layers and piping across all owned code; current portable rules plus proved corrections for remaining gaps | Mutation/loop restrictions, state ownership and precise host exceptions |\\n212:| Website connection | Agreed in Q9 | Native Effect RPC to the same-stage backend; temporarily send calculation facts in a body | RPC contract/version, server binding/browser URL, failure and cancellation proof |\\n213-| Calculation trigger | Agreed in Q10 | Explicit Calculate action; edits invalidate the old answer and interrupt old work | Form/result state and one usage event per successful action |\\n214-| Result explanation | Agreed in Q11 | Main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and rule sources | Accessible result layout and checked explanation repr…2334 tokens truncated…ct owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n  \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"bun run docs:validate\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:docs\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:runbooks\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run build\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check-types\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n    \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\\\",\\n    \\\"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n    \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n    \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n    \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n    \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n    \\\"required\\\": true,\\n    \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n    \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n    \\\"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\\\",\\n    \\\"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\\\",\\n    \\\"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\\\",\\n    \\\"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\\\",\\n    \\\"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true,\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": [\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-compiled-content-contract.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-native-docs-catalogue-source.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-page-copy-review.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-docs-links.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-acceptance.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-content-http.json\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-native-docs-connection.json\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T006\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Add remote MCP and visible browser agent tools\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"vertical-slice\\\",\\n  \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n  \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n    \\\"CSF-005\\\",\\n    \\\"CSF-006\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n    \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n    \\\"CSF-T005\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"goal\\\": \\\"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": [\\n    \\\"Add native Effect remote MCP for catalogue/docs discovery, checked calculator inputs, execution and results, reusing the same named operations and accepted Markdown.\\\",\\n    \\\"Select and qualify native Effect v2026_07_28 stateless and v2025_11_25 stateful adapters before advertising them. Apply anonymous request limits, allowed origins, bounded request/stream lifetimes, cancellation, typed errors and safe tool descriptions; publish discovery and setup docs.\\\",\\n    \\\"Register feature-detected page-owned WebMCP tools for find/read/fill/calculate/read-result. Reuse visible website commands and the checked RPC client; unregister/cancel on route change or unmount. Do not add direct SDK/backend calls or a duplicate calculation/event owner.\\\",\\n    \\\"Document actual browser support and distinguish protocol/schema registration from a real agent journey; ordinary browser use must keep working.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n    \\\"apps/api native MCP adapter and justified contract exports at the existing package owners\\\",\\n    \\\"apps/web page-owned WebMCP registration/command owner and cleanup tests\\\",\\n    \\\"Public agent setup/Markdown docs, app/package READMEs, owning architecture and critical-journey updates\\\",\\n    \\\"HTTP/MCP/WebMCP equality, origin/rate/cancellation and browser evidence\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n  \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"bun run test\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run test:oxlint\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check-types\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run build\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:docs\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n    \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"Exercise browser tools with the supported experimental browser/agent when available, including visible form changes and results.\\\",\\n    \\\"Verify fallback in an unsupported browser, cleanup after navigation, cancellation and equivalent results to manual UI/API.\\\",\\n    \\\"Run a real MCP client for each advertised adapter: current-version per-request metadata/list/read/call; older-version initialise/session/list/read/call. Prove version/header agreement, unsupported versions, origins/rates, real Worker session routing/expiry, streaming cancellation and cleanup; persist no tax figures in session metadata.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n    \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n    \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n    \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n    \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n    \\\"required\\\": true,\\n    \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n    \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n    \\\"Tool names, schemas and descriptions reflect current catalogue/content and use the same calculation owner.\\\",\\n    \\\"Remote and browser tools have actual caller evidence; lack of a supported browser is recorded as a proof gap, never a passed agent journey.\\\",\\n    \\\"Anonymous access has bounded work and no required account or stored calculation.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true\\n}\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T007\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Prepare DNS, domain and secret provider plans\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"vertical-slice\\\",\\n  \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n  \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n    \\\"CSF-007\\\",\\n    \\\"CSF-010\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n    \\\"CSF-T003\\\",\\n    \\\"CSF-T005\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"goal\\\": \\\"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": [\\n    \\\"Read actual taxkit.dev zone/account, records, domain/registrar and DNSSEC state; classify existing state and preserve unrelated mail/verification records.\\\",\\n    \\\"Declare adopted retained Production zone/settings and native taxkit.dev Website plus www redirect and api.taxkit.dev backend domain attachments; keep Preview away from Production DNS. Derive each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, with application-ingress Schema checks and checked failure for absent Outputs. Qualify local, Preview and custom-domain behaviour; domains are infrastructure inputs, not duplicated application-origin configuration.\\\",\\n    \\\"Complete native Doppler stage selection, shell-source policy, named runtime bindings and distinct deploy/query/Turbo credentials; remove stale --env-file wrappers only with equivalent behaviour.\\\",\\n    \\\"Produce version-matched no-apply plans and authority/rollback/readback procedures. Replace graph validators/workflow projection assumptions that admit only one DocsWebsite without adding a bespoke parallel deployment framework.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n    \\\"packages/infrastructure native zone/domain/stage/secrets graph and root alchemy entries\\\",\\n    \\\"tools/docs-deployment/** owning admission/secret/workflow replacements, relevant workflows and Turbo inputs\\\",\\n    \\\"docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md, recovery.md, operations/authority-model.md and tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json\\\",\\n    \\\"Redacted exact-resource plans, retention and DNS/secret readback procedures\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n  \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"bun run check:docs-deployment:types\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:docs-deployment-tools:types\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:docs-deployment\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run test:docs-deployment\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:runbooks\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:repository-paths\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n    \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserVerification\\\": [],\\n  \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n    \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n    \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n    \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n    \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n    \\\"required\\\": true,\\n    \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n    \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n    \\\"The reviewed plan names exact resources/account/stage and never creates or edits Production DNS for a Preview.\\\",\\n    \\\"Doppler precedence, runtime binding and separate credential purposes have checked proof without secret values in output.\\\",\\n    \\\"All cloud mutations remain unexecuted until the concrete plan has the required named authority; DNS/TLS/registrar readback is separate from apply success.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true\\n}\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"CSF-T008\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Implement minimal PostHog traffic and calculator analytics\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"vertical-slice\\\",\\n  \\\"acceptedFindingIds\\\": [],\\n  \\\"requirementIds\\\": [\\n    \\\"CSF-008\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dependsOn\\\": [\\n    \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n    \\\"CSF-T005\\\",\\n    \\\"CSF-T006\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"goal\\\": \\\"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\\\",\\n  \\\"scope\\\": [\\n    \\\"Manage retained TaxKit Production and shared Preview projects through a private Alchemy Resource/Provider and current Distilled PostHog, with checked organisation/region/ownership and safe management failures.\\\",\\n    \\\"Implement explicit pageviews in a private React-owned browser service and one successful hosted-calculation event owner in the backend application; honour a checked browser opt-out without linking identities.\\\",\\n    \\\"Use a synchronous final-enrichment allowlist, memory-only persistence, explicit DNT and disabled automatic/replay/person features. Local and ordinary Preview capture stay off; no consent dialog.\\\",\\n    \\\"Implement the bounded same-origin event relay and native backend capture through owned Effect HTTP. Qualify actual current SDK transport/disposal and no duplicate events; retain best-effort delivery limits.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"outputs\\\": [\\n    \\\"apps/web analytics service/live adapter/consumer/relay and route event ownership\\\",\\n    \\\"apps/api application successful-use capture and checked collection policy\\\",\\n    \\\"packages/infrastructure PostHog provider/resources/bindings and qualified optional provider fixes\\\",\\n    \\\"Analytics tests, app/infra READMEs, privacy/public copy and deployment/recovery runbook sections\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n  \\\"mandatoryVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"bun run test\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run test:oxlint\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check-types\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run build\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:docs\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run check:runbooks\\\",\\n    \\\"bun run verification\\\",\\n    \\\"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"browserVerification\\\": [\\n    \\\"Inspect actual latest-SDK batches for only accepted page/calculator properties, no amounts/results/queries and no extra SDK endpoints.\\\",\\n    \\\"Prove initial/client navigation counts including A-to-B-to-A, one successful-use event per action across UI/WebMCP/API/MCP, no event on failure/cancellation, and backend browser opt-out.\\\",\\n    \\\"Check denied storage, DNT before/after acquisition, ordinary Preview/development off, cleanup and relay size/deadline/status/redirect failures.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"qualityAudits\\\": [\\n    \\\"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\\\",\\n    \\\"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\\\",\\n    \\\"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\\\",\\n    \\\"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"parentAudit\\\": {\\n    \\\"required\\\": true,\\n    \\\"basis\\\": \\\"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\\\",\\n    \\\"recovery\\\": \\\"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"completionCriteria\\\": [\\n    \\\"Only the documented events and fields leave the app; no persistent browser identity or consent dialogue is introduced.\\\",\\n    \\\"One backend owner emits each successful hosted calculator use; pure packages/local SDK calculations send no analytics.\\\",\\n    \\\"An event delivery response is transport proof only; exact provider UUID readback remains a separately authorised Preview journey.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"commitAfterPassing\\\": true\\n}\\n\"}}\n{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"be07af\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005291,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":55,\"output\":\"web test:native-pair: \\nweb test:native-pair:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\\nweb test:native-pair: \\n2372:      // The test scope restores the real owner even if the actual CLI assertion\\n\"}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791301956.512553