],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","realtime_active":false}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac51e12f71087d0a35ff81343106c9f","order":1021,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a111fd-7e14-7e81-9665-088bab7e7522","text":"Both unused-code checks now pass with that schema kept private. The corrected version is going through the complete checks; its page layout and behaviour are unchanged.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac51f6b6e6c87d0a0870e0215a2c6b6","order":1022,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a11202-c012-7903-93a7-b86fa8d63f08","text":"The corrected version has passed all repository tests again. I’ve recorded the earlier failed check and the small correction in the evidence, alongside the successful results.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac5202e9d0087d090d61756b0bb1ccb","order":1023,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a11205-bbe6-73f3-90ca-66c93b2a88da","text":"The remaining checks are taking time because they test deliberately broken copies in separate checkouts. The website’s normal tests and both unused-code checks have passed. I’ll push the page update once this final run finishes.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac520d0306087d0a992dcc59105425f","order":1025,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a11208-30be-7963-a5dc-c54fe9232f28","text":"The standalone browser tests followed a server-only import from the new documentation route. I’m changing how the route receives its page-loading function, then checking those browser tests directly before another full run.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac522d5c57c87d08eed10e08465a553","order":1026,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a11210-1b6e-7b60-bb81-1688d194e331","text":"The corrected setup passes all 20 standalone browser tests and all 11 tests against the built website and API. The documentation routes now use the same application-supplied loading pattern as settings. I’m starting the final combined checks on these files.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac52525329c87d09f511a979fba5c91","order":1027,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a11219-220d-7f91-8ad4-3874617f87ab","text":"All repository tests pass with the corrected page-loading setup. The final clean-checkout checks are running again; after they finish, the remaining steps are the evidence checks and draft PR update.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac5256c768087d0a2f39c6e2e89e565","order":1029,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1121a-3375-7190-bac3-9f0eaf8ce3bf","text":"The clean-checkout checks and both browser test suites have passed. The final freshly built website and API tests are running now.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac52644123c87d0aa1359819b594050","order":1031,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1121d-7fce-70d3-ab30-85d1783a7ff0","text":"The complete checks passed, including the fresh native browser run. I’m recording the final evidence and pushing this documentation-page slice to draft PR #155. Search remains next, and metrics stay on hold.","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":1032,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96db813b1de3","order":0,"revision":"retained_01a1055e-500d-7de0-b833-96f424cd39df","text":"\n# Files pasted by the user:\n\n## \"--- document_type: execution-plan lifecycle: current authority: supporting owne…\": /Users/cooper/.codex/attachments/f82088a9-b579-462a-9bee-4d3685805660/Pasted text.txt\n\nPasted text contains the user's request.\n\n## My request:\n\n","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d613ca83284b","order":162,"revision":"retained_01a106da-6a9d-7e63-a676-d63d307e199e","text":"Continue","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0aa97ccc7c9","order":644,"revision":"retained_01a10eaa-f994-7390-bfc4-e0c71863ea13","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_1bVTWMcCf1Qh4ZCVQoDmUT9n\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"The Linear connector requires a fresh confirmation to post the prepared progress comment to DEV-75. It links draft #146 and its passing checks, and says rate limiting and domain work remain unfinished. Approve this comment?\",\"answer\":\"Approve the DEV-75 comment\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a10fd9-c29b-7150-b630-8c47988f200d","order":825,"revision":"retained_01a10fd9-c29b-7150-b630-8c6f7108e6ae","text":"We are likely to change the metrics approach, so leave this for now and proceed\n","turn_id":"01a10fab-f789-7f30-a7de-963ccee8ae9f"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a11111-19f6-7923-83d8-8844f4e64aec","order":929,"revision":"retained_01a11111-19f6-7923-83d8-886f828f067b","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"answer\":\"Approve the DEV-76 update\",\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_IfjoO3zN1anlISjAhlvKOxDG\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"The Linear connector requires a fresh confirmation to mark DEV-76 In Progress and replace its old planning-only note with the tested PR #155 progress and metrics deferral. Approve this prepared issue update?\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9"}],"user_messages_incomplete":false,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a11227-73f1-7233-8cc5-d81d3861140a","window_number":65}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:58:57.910Z","ordinal":48689,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","text":"## Strict communication requirement\n\nAlways respond in plain, simple Australian English. Use an ELI5 style and avoid jargon, buzzwords, and unexplained technical terms.\n\nThis rule applies especially when discussing codebases or software engineering. Explain those topics in simple English for a beginner unless the user asks for more detail. Use concrete words and examples. Avoid specialist shorthand and vague terms such as “seams” and “gates” unless the user asks for them or the term is essential and clearly explained.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n---\ndocument_type: agent-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: repository-maintainers\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\n---\n\n# TaxKit repository guide\n\nTaxKit is the public monorepo for the open-source tax engine, API, SDK, and\ndocumentation site. Start with [`docs/README.md`](docs/README.md), the sole\nmaintainer-document lifecycle and truth-layer router. `CLAUDE.md` points to this\nfile; edit `AGENTS.md` only.\n\n## Operating loop\n\n1. Read `docs/README.md`, then only the semantic owner for the task.\n2. Confirm the claim against code, configuration, Schemas, exports, generated\n   owners, or external readback at the boundary it describes.\n3. Put current implementation intent in a SPEC/task and active execution plan;\n   never reopen completed work as policy.\n4. Update the earliest durable owner and required pointers in the same slice.\n5. Run `bun run check:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks` when operations changed,\n   focused checks, and `bun run verification`;\n   package-facing changes also need an appropriate Changeset.\n6. Retain artifact identity, authority, postconditions, limitations,\n   non-claims, and rollback.\n\nFor any material calculator/rule/schema, SDK/export/example, HTTP/OpenAPI,\npublic MDX/navigation/runtime, package/app, command/CI/versioning/release-proof,\nlifecycle, SPEC, plan, runbook, or skill change, invoke the repository-local\n`$docs-maintainer` route before accepting the slice. Record `Change required`,\n`Preserve`, or evidenced `N/A` for its documentation impact. Scheduled or\nbackground freshness work is report-only candidate output unless a separately\nattached implementation authority names the reviewer and publisher.\n\n## Task routes\n\n- Repository and package topology:\n  [`docs/architecture/README.md`](docs/architecture/README.md), then\n  [`docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`](docs/architecture/package-ownership.md).\n- Effect services and boundaries:\n  [`docs/architecture/effect-services.md`](docs/architecture/effect-services.md)\n  and the applicable package README.\n- API/SDK: [`docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`](docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md),\n  [`apps/api/README.md`](apps/api/README.md), and\n  [`packages/sdk/typescript/README.md`](packages/sdk/typescript/README.md).\n- Calculators/rules/facts: the focused owner under `docs/architecture/` and the\n  owning package README.\n- Frontend/public docs:\n  [`docs/architecture/frontend.md`](docs/architecture/frontend.md),\n  [`docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md`](docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md),\n  and [`apps/docs/README.md`](apps/docs/README.md).\n- Current work: [`docs/product-specs/index.md`](docs/product-specs/index.md) and\n  [`docs/exec-plans/active/README.md`](docs/exec-plans/active/README.md).\n- Standards, tests, and release checks:\n  [`docs/standards/README.md`](docs/standards/README.md) and\n  [`docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md).\n- Repeatable release, versioning, packed-consumer and recovery operations:\n  [`docs/runbooks/README.md`](docs/runbooks/README.md) and\n  [`docs/operations/authority-model.md`](docs/operations/authority-model.md).\n- References and audits: [`docs/references/README.md`](docs/references/README.md)\n  and [`docs/documentation-audit/README.md`](docs/documentation-audit/README.md).\n\nUse the repository-owned [Linear skill](.agents/skills/linear/SKILL.md) when\nwork is tracked in Linear. The [strict Effect skill](.agents/skills/strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md)\nand [Alchemy skill](.agents/skills/alchemy-iac/SKILL.md) supply methods; local\nprofiles and the installed dependency graph own TaxKit compatibility. Skill\ninstallation does not imply that the clean-slate enforcement migration is complete.\n\n## Engineering guardrails\n\n- Use Effect-native Schema, branded identities, Config, services, Layers,\n  tagged errors, collections, Command, and runtime primitives when they own the\n  semantics. Decode unknown/representation ingress once and encode egress at\n  explicit boundaries.\n- Reuse owning Schemas and schema-derived types. Do not mirror raw `id: string`,\n  DTOs, provider types, primitive semantic config, or unchecked SDK output.\n- Keep primary Effects flat, sequential, and pipe-first where that clarifies\n  data flow. Keep one-use mapping/decoding/error logic inline; reject\n  helper/common/utils sprawl and generic SDK callback wrappers.\n- Keep service contracts, live Layers, test Layers, and executable composition\n  separate. Do not run Effects or build live Layers inside domain logic.\n- Provider clients expose named Effect operations, `Config.schema` with\n  redacted secrets, immediate Schema decoding, safe tagged errors without\n  `instanceof`, and live/mock Layers.\n- React composition flows route → policy-owning container → focused leaf.\n  Routes own transport restoration/outcome matching, containers own commands\n  and coordination, and leaves render readonly values/local interaction state.\n- Admit an abstraction only with semantic weight, an owner, a real reuse or\n  substitution point, a simpler call graph, and focused proof.\n\n## Authority and proof\n\nTool access is capability, not authority. Provider, registry, publication,\nrelease, deployment, credential, and destructive operations require a named\nprincipal, operation, resource, environment, approval boundary, receipt,\nrollback/revocation, and readback. Local gates do not prove publication,\nproduction, or external consumer behavior.\n\nUse `bun run check:repository-paths` for checkout portability and\n`bun run verification` for repository closeout. Use `bun run release:check`\nonly for its documented local release-evidence graph; it does not authorize or\nprove publication.\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","instructions":"0a11049b0421e1e86f1e129af8d547a89548a0c3"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-10-07","timezone":"Australia/Melbourne","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"<agent name=\"/root/impeccable_documenter\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/impeccable_finish_reviewer\" />"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/commonplace/development-workflows/0.6.2/skills`\n- `r4` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/commonplace/foundations/0.5.1/skills`\n- `r5` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r6` = `/Users/cooper/.codex/plu