{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:59:53.654Z","ordinal":48746,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-246cc324-a4eb-4dd4-baf0-4507dd0349fd","process_id":"18496","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1575,1625p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json && cat tools/repository-paths/check.runtime.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1575,1625p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json","name":"2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json","path":"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat tools/repository-paths/check.runtime.ts","name":"check.runtime.ts","path":"tools/repository-paths/check.runtime.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"      \"sha256\": \"653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c\",\n      \"bytes\": 255635,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-desktop.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-mobile.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d\",\n      \"bytes\": 216877,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-mobile.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-diagram-desktop.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc\",\n      \"bytes\": 284215,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-diagram-desktop.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-diagram-mobile.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b\",\n      \"bytes\": 236806,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-diagram-mobile.png\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"designDocumentation\": {\n    \"reviewer\": \"Fresh independent impeccable_documenter\",\n    \"outcome\": \"Ordinary incumbent-system extension; no new design guide required\",\n    \"reportPath\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-design-documentation.md\",\n    \"reportSha256\": \"df7b84de88e3974e2831e22c010d230040c43b2770a771c9746a5237f1d089b8\",\n    \"report\": \"# DEV-76 / CSF-T005 design documentation check\\n\\nDate: 7 October 2026. Mode: Read. Outcome: preserve the existing design.\\n\\nOnly this temporary report was written. No repository file, design guide,\\nprovider or public site was changed by this pass.\\n\\nThe new documentation pages extend the existing Website. The stylesheet at\\nHEAD and the working stylesheet have the same original 184 lines; the diff\\nonly adds document styles. The background, main text, font stack, top\\nnavigation, form styles and keyboard focus colour remain as they were.\\n\\n## Five-line system summary\\n\\n1. Palette: pale background (#f8fafc), dark text (#172033), quieter navigation text (#526071), light borders (#d6dde7), inherited blue focus (#2563eb), and document links in darker blue (#075985).\\n2. Type: the existing Inter/system font stack; article text (1.0625rem, line height 1.75); page title (clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem), line height 1.15); navigation and tables (0.9375rem); code blocks (0.875rem, line height 1.6).\\n3. Layout: article width capped at 72ch, meaning about 72 characters per line; a 17rem desktop sidebar; one column below 52rem; a native collapsible navigation list on phones.\\n4. Surfaces: plain background, thin borders, rounded code blocks (0.375rem), locally scrolling code and tables, and no added shadows or decorative imagery.\\n5. Named rules: no existing named visual rules were found and none were invented; preserve authored reading order, ordinary links, clear current-page marking and visible keyboard focus.\\n\\n## Evidence checked\\n\\nRepository root: `/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit`.\\nBase HEAD: `049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e`.\\nThe checked artifact includes uncommitted work; HEAD alone does not identify it.\\n\\nThe operating instructions read were:\\n\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/document.md`, in full.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/agents/impeccable_documenter.toml`.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/degraded/documenter.md` for comparison with the shipped role. This pass used the actual delegated documenter role; no inline substitution was needed.\\n- The supplied repository `AGENTS.md` instructions, `docs/README.md`, `docs/architecture/frontend.md`, and the repository-local docs-maintainer skill, profile and its document-class, change-impact and proof references.\\n- Current documentation-route notes in `apps/web/README.md`, `docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md` and the active clean-slate plan.\\n\\nThe product source sampled was:\\n\\n| Source | SHA-256 at this pass | Observation |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `apps/web/src/styles.css` | `79c3834a0e88ff1a45a3cbfffef7fec11d740526e60c477d9a2334667e52eb83` | Compared with `git show HEAD:apps/web/src/styles.css` and its actual diff. All original rules are preserved; document rules are appended. |\\n| `apps/web/src/routes/$.tsx` | `3dd5b7088e0052b7976d5c671ba1ee3a9b38cfbe853cc0f8bc6f732659608610` | Sidebar and article remain visible in the route composition; loading, missing-page and unavailable states have clear copy; the article ends with a Markdown link. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/components.tsx` | `7a424f687699e4b672e5e6f5360e014594bc6efa6591966f3f84ac17b43182a5` | Internal page links retain navigation behaviour and deliberate heading focus. The table has a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll area. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/page.view.tsx` | `9ff7a422914f9da0d9d7909b7c77cfd24e931912fbb1b1fab6cbc417dc8f9b37` | Native details/summary navigation, checked page labels and explicit current-page marking. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/mdx.boundary.tsx` | `7efcc5e0249fc5b258bf367f5354dd3d7ac3615b7763b9b802c0873d23218173` | Uses compiled authored pages, checks their text and metadata against the accepted page, and supplies fixed reload guidance for mismatches. |\\n\\nFour saved local captures were visually inspected. Their hashes match the\\ncurrent dated receipt:\\n\\n| Capture under `.alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/` | SHA-256 |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `docs-desktop.png` | `653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c` |\\n| `docs-mobile.png` | `2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d` |\\n| `docs-diagram-desktop.png` | `34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc` |\\n| `docs-diagram-mobile.png` | `d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b` |\\n\\nThe Quickstart and the \\u201cWhat are you changing?\\u201d page show their titles and\\nopening text at the top. The desktop sidebar, phone disclosure, underlined\\ndocument links, code blocks, table and keyboard focus match the source. No\\nblank or broken page region was observed in these captures.\\n\\nThe independent reviewer report at\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-finish-review.md` was read. Its SHA-256 is\\n`2742e01cd53393e748bfa1d9ca74b45b016621bb825dbc3f5898e6c07e07ef35`.\\nIt records `disposition: ship` and no material fixes for this reading and\\nnavigation extension.\\n\\nBefore reading product source, this pass checked\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-focus-a-results.jsonl`: `oxlint-tests` had\\nfinished with exit code 0. This respected the temporary source-replacement\\nwarning supplied with the task.\\n\\nThe saved native test log\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-native-l-native.log` records 7 passing test\\nfiles, 11 passing cases and exit code 0. This pass read that result; it did not\\nrerun the tests or operate a live browser. The dated source receipt at\\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json`\\nrecords 61 accepted pages, preserved navigation, retained integration\\ntemplates and retained calculator outputs. This design pass sampled two pages\\nand did not independently audit every content hash or tax result.\\n\\n## Documentation decision\\n\\n| Surface | Decision | Reason |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Existing Website visual system | Preserve | The original stylesheet is unchanged and the accepted brief requires an ordinary extension. |\\n| PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md and `.impeccable/design.json` | Preserve absence | A repository search found no matching design files. No new visual identity or system change was approved, so the documenter role does not require their creation. Missing files are context, not a failure. |\\n| Authored pages, navigation, examples and tax figures | Preserve | The supplied scope retains these owners; no content change was authorised for this pass. |\\n| Website README, frontend/content architecture and active T005 work | Preserve | These existing owners already describe the page connection and its unfinished work. This pass adds no durable implementation rule. |\\n| Generated references, API/SDK contract, release notes and Changesets | N/A | This pass changes no package, public contract, generator, version or release claim. |\\n| Runbooks, provider state, credentials, CI and publication | N/A | No operational action or external change is part of this pass. |\\n| This isolated evidence report | Change required | The delegated task explicitly requests a record of the design check at this exact temporary path. |\\n\\n## Limits and existing missing context\\n\\nNo PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, approved visual comp, quality card or approved system\\nchange was supplied. The incumbent source and explicit Read-mode extension\\nbrief give enough context for this check. No new brand metaphor, invented\\ndesign rule or replacement design file was introduced.\\n\\nThe diagram lettering is too small to read when fitted to the phone width.\\nThe readable table directly below gives the same choices and destinations;\\nthe reviewer accepted that solution. Small diagram lettering is recorded as a\\nlocal limitation, not a design rule for future pages to copy.\\n\\nThe dated receipt currently still calls full qualification and fresh review\\npending, while its embedded reviewer result says ship. This pre-existing\\nrecord mismatch was reported to the parent agent for the existing closeout\\nwork. It was not repaired by this read-only design pass. No other material\\nvisual drift was found in the sampled source or captures.\\n\\nSearch, discovery files, Markdown negotiation, share images and retirement of\\nthe old documentation app remain unfinished T005 work. Metrics remain\\ndeferred. This report establishes no deployment, public availability,\\npublication, complete repository qualification or external consumer result.\\n\\n```yaml\\ncandidate:\\n  source: The five sampled source files, incumbent HEAD stylesheet, four saved captures and named review/test records listed above.\\n  provenance: Delegated Impeccable documenter read-only comparison.\\n  freshness: Checked on 7 October 2026; source and capture hashes are listed above.\\n  classification: Supporting local design evidence; no system change.\\n  audience: Parent agent and Cooper.\\n  attachedEvidence: The exact source, capture, review and test paths listed above.\\n  proposedSemanticOwner: Existing Website source and frontend/content architecture; no new owner proposed.\\n  targetRevision: Base 049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e plus the sampled uncommitted source hashes above.\\n  unresolvedContradictions: Existing receipt says qualification/review pending while its embedded reviewer result says ship.\\n  responsibleReviewer: Parent agent for this supporting report; independent finish reviewer for the supplied ship decision.\\n  publisherIdentity: Unknown; no publication is requested or authorised by this pass.\\n  publicationStatus: Not published; isolated temporary report only.\\n  revocationQuarantine: Disregard this report if any sampled source changes; repeat the comparison before reuse.\\n  lastKnownGoodRecovery: Retain incumbent source; this pass has no repository mutation to roll back.\\n  postPublicationReadback: N/A; this pass performs no publication.\\n```\\n\\nNot made into a rule or repaired: the phone diagram's tiny text and the existing\\npending receipt wording, because this pass only records the accepted design\\nextension and leaves the owning closeout work with the parent agent.\\n\",\n    \"writeBoundary\": \"Temporary report only; repository design files preserved\",\n    \"laterCorrectionReview\": \"Styles, MDX components and rendered composition are unchanged. A later route loader correction uses the typed application router context; no visual system change.\"\n  },\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex under Cooper approved T005 implementation authority\",\n    \"decision\": \"Accepted bounded Website page/navigation slice with complete local qualification; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n    \"findings\": [\n      \"One owning application runtime; named docs client operations remain separate from private calculator admission.\",\n      \"Native byte request adapter keeps binding receiver and signal; response decoded immediately; safe tagged errors discard provider diagnostics.\",\n      \"Dedicated route decoder and direct first consumers; visible route composition and readonly focused leaves; no generic wrapper/provider or browser runner.\",\n      \"Installed MDX compiler and browser-safe presentation imports; body/metadata/module mismatches have actual cold native proof.\",\n      \"Exact lint decoder/class-factory admissions with neighbouring renderer/runtime/encoder restrictions exercised by 591 actual-command tests.\",\n      \"Source-built fault fixtures restore exact API/live-layer owners; real native HTML and Chromium prevent checked-value-only imitation.\",\n      \"Retained source/template/tax outputs and disabled collection remain; no new package export contract, Changeset or external operation.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"failedQualification\": [\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"all-tests\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"run\",\nimport * as BunRuntime from \"@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime\";\nimport * as BunServices from \"@effect/platform-bun/BunServices\";\nimport { Array, Console, Effect, Match, Option, Schema, Stream } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FileSystem from \"effect/FileSystem\";\nimport { pipe } from \"effect/Function\";\nimport * as Path from \"effect/Path\";\nimport { ChildProcess, ChildProcessSpawner } from \"effect/process\";\n\nimport {\n  decodeReadableRepositoryText,\n  inspectRepositoryText,\n  createRepositoryPathReport,\n  renderRepositoryPathReport,\n} from \"./policy.js\";\nimport {\n  RepositoryFileReadError,\n  RepositoryInventoryError,\n  RepositoryPolicyViolationError,\n  RepositoryRelativeFile,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\n\nconst repositoryRootUrl = new URL(\"../..\", import.meta.url);\nconst TrackedFileInventory = Schema.Array(RepositoryRelativeFile);\n\nexport const checkRepositoryPaths = (repositoryRoot: string) =>\n  Effect.gen(function* checkTrackedRepositoryText() {\n    const childProcesses = yield* ChildProcessSpawner.ChildProcessSpawner;\n    const fileSystem = yield* FileSystem.FileSystem;\n    const path = yield* Path.Path;\n\n    const inventory = yield* Effect.gen(function* listTrackedFiles() {\n      const handle = yield* childProcesses.spawn(\n        ChildProcess.make(\"git\", [\"ls-files\", \"-z\"], {\n          cwd: repositoryRoot,\n          extendEnv: true,\n          forceKillAfter: \"2 seconds\",\n          stderr: \"pipe\",\n          stdin: \"ignore\",\n          stdout: \"pipe\",\n        })\n      );\n      const [stdout, [exitCode]] = yield* Effect.all(\n        [\n          Stream.runCollect(handle.stdout),\n          Effect.zip(handle.exitCode, Stream.runDrain(handle.stderr), {\n            concurrent: true,\n          }),\n        ],\n        { concurrency: \"unbounded\" }\n      );\n\n      yield* Match.value(Number(exitCode)).pipe(\n        Match.when(0, () => Effect.void),\n        Match.orElse((code) =>\n          Effect.fail(\n            new RepositoryInventoryError({\n              exitCode: code,\n              operation: \"list-tracked-files\",\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      );\n\n      const bytes = Uint8Array.from(Array.flatMap(stdout, Array.fromIterable));\n      const decoded = yield* Effect.try({\n        catch: () =>\n          new RepositoryInventoryError({\n            operation: \"decode-tracked-files\",\n          }),\n        try: () => new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true }).decode(bytes),\n      });\n\n      return yield* pipe(\n        decoded.split(\"\\0\"),\n        Array.filter((file) => file.length > 0),\n        Schema.decodeUnknownEffect(TrackedFileInventory),\n        Effect.mapError(\n          () =>\n            new RepositoryInventoryError({\n              operation: \"decode-tracked-files\",\n            })\n        )\n      );\n    }).pipe(\n      Effect.scoped,\n      Effect.catchTag(\"PlatformError\", () =>\n        Effect.fail(\n          new RepositoryInventoryError({\n            operation: \"list-tracked-files\",\n          })\n        )\n      )\n    );\n\n    const inspected = yield* Effect.forEach(\n      inventory,\n      (file) => {\n        const filePath = path.join(repositoryRoot, file);\n\n        return fileSystem.readLink(filePath).pipe(\n          Effect.map((target) => new TextEncoder().encode(target)),\n          Effect.catchTag(\"PlatformError\", () => fileSystem.readFile(filePath)),\n          Effect.mapError(() => new RepositoryFileReadError({ file })),\n          Effect.map((bytes) =>\n            decodeReadableRepositoryText(bytes).pipe(\n              Option.match({\n                onNone: () => ({ binary: true, findings: [] }),\n                onSome: (text) => ({\n                  binary: false,\n                  findings: inspectRepositoryText(file, text),\n                }),\n              })\n            )\n          )\n        );\n      },\n      { concurrency: 16 }\n    );\n    const binaryFiles = Array.filter(inspected, (file) => file.binary).length;\n\n    return createRepositoryPathReport({\n      binaryFiles,\n      findings: Array.flatMap(inspected, (file) => file.findings),\n      textFiles: inspected.length - binaryFiles,\n      trackedFiles: inventory.length,\n    });\n  });\n\nconst program = Effect.gen(function* repositoryPathMain() {\n  const path = yield* Path.Path;\n  const repositoryRoot = yield* path.fromFileUrl(repositoryRootUrl).pipe(\n    Effect.mapError(\n      () =>\n        new RepositoryInventoryError({\n          operation: \"resolve-repository-root\",\n        })\n    )\n  );\n\n  return yield* checkRepositoryPaths(repositoryRoot);\n}).pipe(\n  Effect.tap((report) => Console.info(renderRepositoryPathReport(report))),\n  Effect.tap((report) =>\n    Match.value(report.findings.length).pipe(\n      Match.when(0, () => Effect.void),\n      Match.orElse(() =>\n        Effect.fail(new RepositoryPolicyViolationError({ report }))\n      )\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryInventoryError\", (error) =>\n    Console.error(\n      `Repository path check failed during ${error.operation}${Option.fromNullishOr(\n        error.exitCode\n      ).pipe(\n        Option.match({\n          onNone: () => \"\",\n          onSome: (exitCode) => ` (exit ${exitCode})`,\n        })\n      )}.`\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryFileReadError\", (error) =>\n    Console.error(`Repository path check could not read ${error.file}.`)\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryPolicyViolationError\", () => Effect.void),\n  Effect.provide(BunServices.layer)\n);\n\nMatch.value(import.meta.main).pipe(\n  Match.when(true, () => BunRuntime.runMain(program)),\n  Match.orElse(() => false)\n);\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"      \"sha256\": \"653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c\",\n      \"bytes\": 255635,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-desktop.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-mobile.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d\",\n      \"bytes\": 216877,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-mobile.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-diagram-desktop.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc\",\n      \"bytes\": 284215,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-diagram-desktop.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-diagram-mobile.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b\",\n      \"bytes\": 236806,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-diagram-mobile.png\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"designDocumentation\": {\n    \"reviewer\": \"Fresh independent impeccable_documenter\",\n    \"outcome\": \"Ordinary incumbent-system extension; no new design guide required\",\n    \"reportPath\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-design-documentation.md\",\n    \"reportSha256\": \"df7b84de88e3974e2831e22c010d230040c43b2770a771c9746a5237f1d089b8\",\n    \"report\": \"# DEV-76 / CSF-T005 design documentation check\\n\\nDate: 7 October 2026. Mode: Read. Outcome: preserve the existing design.\\n\\nOnly this temporary report was written. No repository file, design guide,\\nprovider or public site was changed by this pass.\\n\\nThe new documentation pages extend the existing Website. The stylesheet at\\nHEAD and the working stylesheet have the same original 184 lines; the diff\\nonly adds document styles. The background, main text, font stack, top\\nnavigation, form styles and keyboard focus colour remain as they were.\\n\\n## Five-line system summary\\n\\n1. Palette: pale background (#f8fafc), dark text (#172033), quieter navigation text (#526071), light borders (#d6dde7), inherited blue focus (#2563eb), and document links in darker blue (#075985).\\n2. Type: the existing Inter/system font stack; article text (1.0625rem, line height 1.75); page title (clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem), line height 1.15); navigation and tables (0.9375rem); code blocks (0.875rem, line height 1.6).\\n3. Layout: article width capped at 72ch, meaning about 72 characters per line; a 17rem desktop sidebar; one column below 52rem; a native collapsible navigation list on phones.\\n4. Surfaces: plain background, thin borders, rounded code blocks (0.375rem), locally scrolling code and tables, and no added shadows or decorative imagery.\\n5. Named rules: no existing named visual rules were found and none were invented; preserve authored reading order, ordinary links, clear current-page marking and visible keyboard focus.\\n\\n## Evidence checked\\n\\nRepository root: `/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit`.\\nBase HEAD: `049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e`.\\nThe checked artifact includes uncommitted work; HEAD alone does not identify it.\\n\\nThe operating instructions read were:\\n\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/document.md`, in full.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/agents/impeccable_documenter.toml`.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/degraded/documenter.md` for comparison with the shipped role. This pass used the actual delegated documenter role; no inline substitution was needed.\\n- The supplied repository `AGENTS.md` instructions, `docs/README.md`, `docs/architecture/frontend.md`, and the repository-local docs-maintainer skill, profile and its document-class, change-impact and proof references.\\n- Current documentation-route notes in `apps/web/README.md`, `docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md` and the active clean-slate plan.\\n\\nThe product source sampled was:\\n\\n| Source | SHA-256 at this pass | Observation |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `apps/web/src/styles.css` | `79c3834a0e88ff1a45a3cbfffef7fec11d740526e60c477d9a2334667e52eb83` | Compared with `git show HEAD:apps/web/src/styles.css` and its actual diff. All original rules are preserved; document rules are appended. |\\n| `apps/web/src/routes/$.tsx` | `3dd5b7088e0052b7976d5c671ba1ee3a9b38cfbe853cc0f8bc6f732659608610` | Sidebar and article remain visible in the route composition; loading, missing-page and unavailable states have clear copy; the article ends with a Markdown link. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/components.tsx` | `7a424f687699e4b672e5e6f5360e014594bc6efa6591966f3f84ac17b43182a5` | Internal page links retain navigation behaviour and deliberate heading focus. The table has a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll area. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/page.view.tsx` | `9ff7a422914f9da0d9d7909b7c77cfd24e931912fbb1b1fab6cbc417dc8f9b37` | Native details/summary navigation, checked page labels and explicit current-page marking. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/mdx.boundary.tsx` | `7efcc5e0249fc5b258bf367f5354dd3d7ac3615b7763b9b802c0873d23218173` | Uses compiled authored pages, checks their text and metadata against the accepted page, and supplies fixed reload guidance for mismatches. |\\n\\nFour saved local captures were visually inspected. Their hashes match the\\ncurrent dated receipt:\\n\\n| Capture under `.alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/` | SHA-256 |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `docs-desktop.png` | `653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c` |\\n| `docs-mobile.png` | `2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d` |\\n| `docs-diagram-desktop.png` | `34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc` |\\n| `docs-diagram-mobile.png` | `d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b` |\\n\\nThe Quickstart and the \\u201cWhat are you changing?\\u201d page show their titles and\\nopening text at the top. The desktop sidebar, phone disclosure, underlined\\ndocument links, code blocks, table and keyboard focus match the source. No\\nblank or broken page region was observed in these captures.\\n\\nThe independent reviewer report at\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-finish-review.md` was read. Its SHA-256 is\\n`2742e01cd53393e748bfa1d9ca74b45b016621bb825dbc3f5898e6c07e07ef35`.\\nIt records `disposition: ship` and no material fixes for this reading and\\nnavigation extension.\\n\\nBefore reading product source, this pass checked\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-focus-a-results.jsonl`: `oxlint-tests` had\\nfinished with exit code 0. This respected the temporary source-replacement\\nwarning supplied with the task.\\n\\nThe saved native test log\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-native-l-native.log` records 7 passing test\\nfiles, 11 passing cases and exit code 0. This pass read that result; it did not\\nrerun the tests or operate a live browser. The dated source receipt at\\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json`\\nrecords 61 accepted pages, preserved navigation, retained integration\\ntemplates and retained calculator outputs. This design pass sampled two pages\\nand did not independently audit every content hash or tax result.\\n\\n## Documentation decision\\n\\n| Surface | Decision | Reason |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Existing Website visual system | Preserve | The original stylesheet is unchanged and the accepted brief requires an ordinary extension. |\\n| PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md and `.impeccable/design.json` | Preserve absence | A repository search found no matching design files. No new visual identity or system change was approved, so the documenter role does not require their creation. Missing files are context, not a failure. |\\n| Authored pages, navigation, examples and tax figures | Preserve | The supplied scope retains these owners; no content change was authorised for this pass. |\\n| Website README, frontend/content architecture and active T005 work | Preserve | These existing owners already describe the page connection and its unfinished work. This pass adds no durable implementation rule. |\\n| Generated references, API/SDK contract, release notes and Changesets | N/A | This pass changes no package, public contract, generator, version or release claim. |\\n| Runbooks, provider state, credentials, CI and publication | N/A | No operational action or external change is part of this pass. |\\n| This isolated evidence report | Change required | The delegated task explicitly requests a record of the design check at this exact temporary path. |\\n\\n## Limits and existing missing context\\n\\nNo PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, approved visual comp, quality card or approved system\\nchange was supplied. The incumbent source and explicit Read-mode extension\\nbrief give enough context for this check. No new brand metaphor, invented\\ndesign rule or replacement design file was introduced.\\n\\nThe diagram lettering is too small to read when fitted to the phone width.\\nThe readable table directly below gives the same choices and destinations;\\nthe reviewer accepted that solution. Small diagram lettering is recorded as a\\nlocal limitation, not a design rule for future pages to copy.\\n\\nThe dated receipt currently still calls full qualification and fresh review\\npending, while its embedded reviewer result says ship. This pre-existing\\nrecord mismatch was reported to the parent agent for the existing closeout\\nwork. It was not repaired by this read-only design pass. No other material\\nvisual drift was found in the sampled source or captures.\\n\\nSearch, discovery files, Markdown negotiation, share images and retirement of\\nthe old documentation app remain unfinished T005 work. Metrics remain\\ndeferred. This report establishes no deployment, public availability,\\npublication, complete repository qualification or external consumer result.\\n\\n```yaml\\ncandidate:\\n  source: The five sampled source files, incumbent HEAD stylesheet, four saved captures and named review/test records listed above.\\n  provenance: Delegated Impeccable documenter read-only comparison.\\n  freshness: Checked on 7 October 2026; source and capture hashes are listed above.\\n  classification: Supporting local design evidence; no system change.\\n  audience: Parent agent and Cooper.\\n  attachedEvidence: The exact source, capture, review and test paths listed above.\\n  proposedSemanticOwner: Existing Website source and frontend/content architecture; no new owner proposed.\\n  targetRevision: Base 049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e plus the sampled uncommitted source hashes above.\\n  unresolvedContradictions: Existing receipt says qualification/review pending while its embedded reviewer result says ship.\\n  responsibleReviewer: Parent agent for this supporting report; independent finish reviewer for the supplied ship decision.\\n  publisherIdentity: Unknown; no publication is requested or authorised by this pass.\\n  publicationStatus: Not published; isolated temporary report only.\\n  revocationQuarantine: Disregard this report if any sampled source changes; repeat the comparison before reuse.\\n  lastKnownGoodRecovery: Retain incumbent source; this pass has no repository mutation to roll back.\\n  postPublicationReadback: N/A; this pass performs no publication.\\n```\\n\\nNot made into a rule or repaired: the phone diagram's tiny text and the existing\\npending receipt wording, because this pass only records the accepted design\\nextension and leaves the owning closeout work with the parent agent.\\n\",\n    \"writeBoundary\": \"Temporary report only; repository design files preserved\",\n    \"laterCorrectionReview\": \"Styles, MDX components and rendered composition are unchanged. A later route loader correction uses the typed application router context; no visual system change.\"\n  },\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex under Cooper approved T005 implementation authority\",\n    \"decision\": \"Accepted bounded Website page/navigation slice with complete local qualification; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n    \"findings\": [\n      \"One owning application runtime; named docs client operations remain separate from private calculator admission.\",\n      \"Native byte request adapter keeps binding receiver and signal; response decoded immediately; safe tagged errors discard provider diagnostics.\",\n      \"Dedicated route decoder and direct first consumers; visible route composition and readonly focused leaves; no generic wrapper/provider or browser runner.\",\n      \"Installed MDX compiler and browser-safe presentation imports; body/metadata/module mismatches have actual cold native proof.\",\n      \"Exact lint decoder/class-factory admissions with neighbouring renderer/runtime/encoder restrictions exercised by 591 actual-command tests.\",\n      \"Source-built fault fixtures restore exact API/live-layer owners; real native HTML and Chromium prevent checked-value-only imitation.\",\n      \"Retained source/template/tax outputs and disabled collection remain; no new package export contract, Changeset or external operation.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"failedQualification\": [\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"all-tests\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"run\",\nimport * as BunRuntime from \"@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime\";\nimport * as BunServices from \"@effect/platform-bun/BunServices\";\nimport { Array, Console, Effect, Match, Option, Schema, Stream } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FileSystem from \"effect/FileSystem\";\nimport { pipe } from \"effect/Function\";\nimport * as Path from \"effect/Path\";\nimport { ChildProcess, ChildProcessSpawner } from \"effect/process\";\n\nimport {\n  decodeReadableRepositoryText,\n  inspectRepositoryText,\n  createRepositoryPathReport,\n  renderRepositoryPathReport,\n} from \"./policy.js\";\nimport {\n  RepositoryFileReadError,\n  RepositoryInventoryError,\n  RepositoryPolicyViolationError,\n  RepositoryRelativeFile,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\n\nconst repositoryRootUrl = new URL(\"../..\", import.meta.url);\nconst TrackedFileInventory = Schema.Array(RepositoryRelativeFile);\n\nexport const checkRepositoryPaths = (repositoryRoot: string) =>\n  Effect.gen(function* checkTrackedRepositoryText() {\n    const childProcesses = yield* ChildProcessSpawner.ChildProcessSpawner;\n    const fileSystem = yield* FileSystem.FileSystem;\n    const path = yield* Path.Path;\n\n    const inventory = yield* Effect.gen(function* listTrackedFiles() {\n      const handle = yield* childProcesses.spawn(\n        ChildProcess.make(\"git\", [\"ls-files\", \"-z\"], {\n          cwd: repositoryRoot,\n          extendEnv: true,\n          forceKillAfter: \"2 seconds\",\n          stderr: \"pipe\",\n          stdin: \"ignore\",\n          stdout: \"pipe\",\n        })\n      );\n      const [stdout, [exitCode]] = yield* Effect.all(\n        [\n          Stream.runCollect(handle.stdout),\n          Effect.zip(handle.exitCode, Stream.runDrain(handle.stderr), {\n            concurrent: true,\n          }),\n        ],\n        { concurrency: \"unbounded\" }\n      );\n\n      yield* Match.value(Number(exitCode)).pipe(\n        Match.when(0, () => Effect.void),\n        Match.orElse((code) =>\n          Effect.fail(\n            new RepositoryInventoryError({\n              exitCode: code,\n              operation: \"list-tracked-files\",\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      );\n\n      const bytes = Uint8Array.from(Array.flatMap(stdout, Array.fromIterable));\n      const decoded = yield* Effect.try({\n        catch: () =>\n          new RepositoryInventoryError({\n            operation: \"decode-tracked-files\",\n          }),\n        try: () => new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true }).decode(bytes),\n      });\n\n      return yield* pipe(\n        decoded.split(\"\\0\"),\n        Array.filter((file) => file.length > 0),\n        Schema.decodeUnknownEffect(TrackedFileInventory),\n        Effect.mapError(\n          () =>\n            new RepositoryInventoryError({\n              operation: \"decode-tracked-files\",\n            })\n        )\n      );\n    }).pipe(\n      Effect.scoped,\n      Effect.catchTag(\"PlatformError\", () =>\n        Effect.fail(\n          new RepositoryInventoryError({\n            operation: \"list-tracked-files\",\n          })\n        )\n      )\n    );\n\n    const inspected = yield* Effect.forEach(\n      inventory,\n      (file) => {\n        const filePath = path.join(repositoryRoot, file);\n\n        return fileSystem.readLink(filePath).pipe(\n          Effect.map((target) => new TextEncoder().encode(target)),\n          Effect.catchTag(\"PlatformError\", () => fileSystem.readFile(filePath)),\n          Effect.mapError(() => new RepositoryFileReadError({ file })),\n          Effect.map((bytes) =>\n            decodeReadableRepositoryText(bytes).pipe(\n              Option.match({\n                onNone: () => ({ binary: true, findings: [] }),\n                onSome: (text) => ({\n                  binary: false,\n                  findings: inspectRepositoryText(file, text),\n                }),\n              })\n            )\n          )\n        );\n      },\n      { concurrency: 16 }\n    );\n    const binaryFiles = Array.filter(inspected, (file) => file.binary).length;\n\n    return createRepositoryPathReport({\n      binaryFiles,\n      findings: Array.flatMap(inspected, (file) => file.findings),\n      textFiles: inspected.length - binaryFiles,\n      trackedFiles: inventory.length,\n    });\n  });\n\nconst program = Effect.gen(function* repositoryPathMain() {\n  const path = yield* Path.Path;\n  const repositoryRoot = yield* path.fromFileUrl(repositoryRootUrl).pipe(\n    Effect.mapError(\n      () =>\n        new RepositoryInventoryError({\n          operation: \"resolve-repository-root\",\n        })\n    )\n  );\n\n  return yield* checkRepositoryPaths(repositoryRoot);\n}).pipe(\n  Effect.tap((report) => Console.info(renderRepositoryPathReport(report))),\n  Effect.tap((report) =>\n    Match.value(report.findings.length).pipe(\n      Match.when(0, () => Effect.void),\n      Match.orElse(() =>\n        Effect.fail(new RepositoryPolicyViolationError({ report }))\n      )\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryInventoryError\", (error) =>\n    Console.error(\n      `Repository path check failed during ${error.operation}${Option.fromNullishOr(\n        error.exitCode\n      ).pipe(\n        Option.match({\n          onNone: () => \"\",\n          onSome: (exitCode) => ` (exit ${exitCode})`,\n        })\n      )}.`\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryFileReadError\", (error) =>\n    Console.error(`Repository path check could not read ${error.file}.`)\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryPolicyViolationError\", () => Effect.void),\n  Effect.provide(BunServices.layer)\n);\n\nMatch.value(import.meta.main).pipe(\n  Match.when(true, () => BunRuntime.runMain(program)),\n  Match.orElse(() => false)\n);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5833},"formatted_output":"      \"sha256\": \"653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c\",\n      \"bytes\": 255635,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-desktop.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-mobile.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d\",\n      \"bytes\": 216877,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-mobile.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-diagram-desktop.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc\",\n      \"bytes\": 284215,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-diagram-desktop.png\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/docs-diagram-mobile.png\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b\",\n      \"bytes\": 236806,\n      \"reviewedCopy\": \".alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/reviewed/docs-diagram-mobile.png\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"designDocumentation\": {\n    \"reviewer\": \"Fresh independent impeccable_documenter\",\n    \"outcome\": \"Ordinary incumbent-system extension; no new design guide required\",\n    \"reportPath\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-design-documentation.md\",\n    \"reportSha256\": \"df7b84de88e3974e2831e22c010d230040c43b2770a771c9746a5237f1d089b8\",\n    \"report\": \"# DEV-76 / CSF-T005 design documentation check\\n\\nDate: 7 October 2026. Mode: Read. Outcome: preserve the existing design.\\n\\nOnly this temporary report was written. No repository file, design guide,\\nprovider or public site was changed by this pass.\\n\\nThe new documentation pages extend the existing Website. The stylesheet at\\nHEAD and the working stylesheet have the same original 184 lines; the diff\\nonly adds document styles. The background, main text, font stack, top\\nnavigation, form styles and keyboard focus colour remain as they were.\\n\\n## Five-line system summary\\n\\n1. Palette: pale background (#f8fafc), dark text (#172033), quieter navigation text (#526071), light borders (#d6dde7), inherited blue focus (#2563eb), and document links in darker blue (#075985).\\n2. Type: the existing Inter/system font stack; article text (1.0625rem, line height 1.75); page title (clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem), line height 1.15); navigation and tables (0.9375rem); code blocks (0.875rem, line height 1.6).\\n3. Layout: article width capped at 72ch, meaning about 72 characters per line; a 17rem desktop sidebar; one column below 52rem; a native collapsible navigation list on phones.\\n4. Surfaces: plain background, thin borders, rounded code blocks (0.375rem), locally scrolling code and tables, and no added shadows or decorative imagery.\\n5. Named rules: no existing named visual rules were found and none were invented; preserve authored reading order, ordinary links, clear current-page marking and visible keyboard focus.\\n\\n## Evidence checked\\n\\nRepository root: `/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit`.\\nBase HEAD: `049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e`.\\nThe checked artifact includes uncommitted work; HEAD alone does not identify it.\\n\\nThe operating instructions read were:\\n\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/document.md`, in full.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/agents/impeccable_documenter.toml`.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/degraded/documenter.md` for comparison with the shipped role. This pass used the actual delegated documenter role; no inline substitution was needed.\\n- The supplied repository `AGENTS.md` instructions, `docs/README.md`, `docs/architecture/frontend.md`, and the repository-local docs-maintainer skill, profile and its document-class, change-impact and proof references.\\n- Current documentation-route notes in `apps/web/README.md`, `docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md` and the active clean-slate plan.\\n\\nThe product source sampled was:\\n\\n| Source | SHA-256 at this pass | Observation |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `apps/web/src/styles.css` | `79c3834a0e88ff1a45a3cbfffef7fec11d740526e60c477d9a2334667e52eb83` | Compared with `git show HEAD:apps/web/src/styles.css` and its actual diff. All original rules are preserved; document rules are appended. |\\n| `apps/web/src/routes/$.tsx` | `3dd5b7088e0052b7976d5c671ba1ee3a9b38cfbe853cc0f8bc6f732659608610` | Sidebar and article remain visible in the route composition; loading, missing-page and unavailable states have clear copy; the article ends with a Markdown link. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/components.tsx` | `7a424f687699e4b672e5e6f5360e014594bc6efa6591966f3f84ac17b43182a5` | Internal page links retain navigation behaviour and deliberate heading focus. The table has a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll area. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/page.view.tsx` | `9ff7a422914f9da0d9d7909b7c77cfd24e931912fbb1b1fab6cbc417dc8f9b37` | Native details/summary navigation, checked page labels and explicit current-page marking. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/mdx.boundary.tsx` | `7efcc5e0249fc5b258bf367f5354dd3d7ac3615b7763b9b802c0873d23218173` | Uses compiled authored pages, checks their text and metadata against the accepted page, and supplies fixed reload guidance for mismatches. |\\n\\nFour saved local captures were visually inspected. Their hashes match the\\ncurrent dated receipt:\\n\\n| Capture under `.alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/` | SHA-256 |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `docs-desktop.png` | `653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c` |\\n| `docs-mobile.png` | `2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d` |\\n| `docs-diagram-desktop.png` | `34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc` |\\n| `docs-diagram-mobile.png` | `d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b` |\\n\\nThe Quickstart and the \\u201cWhat are you changing?\\u201d page show their titles and\\nopening text at the top. The desktop sidebar, phone disclosure, underlined\\ndocument links, code blocks, table and keyboard focus match the source. No\\nblank or broken page region was observed in these captures.\\n\\nThe independent reviewer report at\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-finish-review.md` was read. Its SHA-256 is\\n`2742e01cd53393e748bfa1d9ca74b45b016621bb825dbc3f5898e6c07e07ef35`.\\nIt records `disposition: ship` and no material fixes for this reading and\\nnavigation extension.\\n\\nBefore reading product source, this pass checked\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-focus-a-results.jsonl`: `oxlint-tests` had\\nfinished with exit code 0. This respected the temporary source-replacement\\nwarning supplied with the task.\\n\\nThe saved native test log\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-native-l-native.log` records 7 passing test\\nfiles, 11 passing cases and exit code 0. This pass read that result; it did not\\nrerun the tests or operate a live browser. The dated source receipt at\\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json`\\nrecords 61 accepted pages, preserved navigation, retained integration\\ntemplates and retained calculator outputs. This design pass sampled two pages\\nand did not independently audit every content hash or tax result.\\n\\n## Documentation decision\\n\\n| Surface | Decision | Reason |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Existing Website visual system | Preserve | The original stylesheet is unchanged and the accepted brief requires an ordinary extension. |\\n| PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md and `.impeccable/design.json` | Preserve absence | A repository search found no matching design files. No new visual identity or system change was approved, so the documenter role does not require their creation. Missing files are context, not a failure. |\\n| Authored pages, navigation, examples and tax figures | Preserve | The supplied scope retains these owners; no content change was authorised for this pass. |\\n| Website README, frontend/content architecture and active T005 work | Preserve | These existing owners already describe the page connection and its unfinished work. This pass adds no durable implementation rule. |\\n| Generated references, API/SDK contract, release notes and Changesets | N/A | This pass changes no package, public contract, generator, version or release claim. |\\n| Runbooks, provider state, credentials, CI and publication | N/A | No operational action or external change is part of this pass. |\\n| This isolated evidence report | Change required | The delegated task explicitly requests a record of the design check at this exact temporary path. |\\n\\n## Limits and existing missing context\\n\\nNo PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, approved visual comp, quality card or approved system\\nchange was supplied. The incumbent source and explicit Read-mode extension\\nbrief give enough context for this check. No new brand metaphor, invented\\ndesign rule or replacement design file was introduced.\\n\\nThe diagram lettering is too small to read when fitted to the phone width.\\nThe readable table directly below gives the same choices and destinations;\\nthe reviewer accepted that solution. Small diagram lettering is recorded as a\\nlocal limitation, not a design rule for future pages to copy.\\n\\nThe dated receipt currently still calls full qualification and fresh review\\npending, while its embedded reviewer result says ship. This pre-existing\\nrecord mismatch was reported to the parent agent for the existing closeout\\nwork. It was not repaired by this read-only design pass. No other material\\nvisual drift was found in the sampled source or captures.\\n\\nSearch, discovery files, Markdown negotiation, share images and retirement of\\nthe old documentation app remain unfinished T005 work. Metrics remain\\ndeferred. This report establishes no deployment, public availability,\\npublication, complete repository qualification or external consumer result.\\n\\n```yaml\\ncandidate:\\n  source: The five sampled source files, incumbent HEAD stylesheet, four saved captures and named review/test records listed above.\\n  provenance: Delegated Impeccable documenter read-only comparison.\\n  freshness: Checked on 7 October 2026; source and capture hashes are listed above.\\n  classification: Supporting local design evidence; no system change.\\n  audience: Parent agent and Cooper.\\n  attachedEvidence: The exact source, capture, review and test paths listed above.\\n  proposedSemanticOwner: Existing Website source and frontend/content architecture; no new owner proposed.\\n  targetRevision: Base 049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e plus the sampled uncommitted source hashes above.\\n  unresolvedContradictions: Existing receipt says qualification/review pending while its embedded reviewer result says ship.\\n  responsibleReviewer: Parent agent for this supporting report; independent finish reviewer for the supplied ship decision.\\n  publisherIdentity: Unknown; no publication is requested or authorised by this pass.\\n  publicationStatus: Not published; isolated temporary report only.\\n  revocationQuarantine: Disregard this report if any sampled source changes; repeat the comparison before reuse.\\n  lastKnownGoodRecovery: Retain incumbent source; this pass has no repository mutation to roll back.\\n  postPublicationReadback: N/A; this pass performs no publication.\\n```\\n\\nNot made into a rule or repaired: the phone diagram's tiny text and the existing\\npending receipt wording, because this pass only records the accepted design\\nextension and leaves the owning closeout work with the parent agent.\\n\",\n    \"writeBoundary\": \"Temporary report only; repository design files preserved\",\n    \"laterCorrectionReview\": \"Styles, MDX components and rendered composition are unchanged. A later route loader correction uses the typed application router context; no visual system change.\"\n  },\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex under Cooper approved T005 implementation authority\",\n    \"decision\": \"Accepted bounded Website page/navigation slice with complete local qualification; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n    \"findings\": [\n      \"One owning application runtime; named docs client operations remain separate from private calculator admission.\",\n      \"Native byte request adapter keeps binding receiver and signal; response decoded immediately; safe tagged errors discard provider diagnostics.\",\n      \"Dedicated route decoder and direct first consumers; visible route composition and readonly focused leaves; no generic wrapper/provider or browser runner.\",\n      \"Installed MDX compiler and browser-safe presentation imports; body/metadata/module mismatches have actual cold native proof.\",\n      \"Exact lint decoder/class-factory admissions with neighbouring renderer/runtime/encoder restrictions exercised by 591 actual-command tests.\",\n      \"Source-built fault fixtures restore exact API/live-layer owners; real native HTML and Chromium prevent checked-value-only imitation.\",\n      \"Retained source/template/tax outputs and disabled collection remain; no new package export contract, Changeset or external operation.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"failedQualification\": [\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"all-tests\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"run\",\nimport * as BunRuntime from \"@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime\";\nimport * as BunServices from \"@effect/platform-bun/BunServices\";\nimport { Array, Console, Effect, Match, Option, Schema, Stream } from \"effect\";\nimport * as FileSystem from \"effect/FileSystem\";\nimport { pipe } from \"effect/Function\";\nimport * as Path from \"effect/Path\";\nimport { ChildProcess, ChildProcessSpawner } from \"effect/process\";\n\nimport {\n  decodeReadableRepositoryText,\n  inspectRepositoryText,\n  createRepositoryPathReport,\n  renderRepositoryPathReport,\n} from \"./policy.js\";\nimport {\n  RepositoryFileReadError,\n  RepositoryInventoryError,\n  RepositoryPolicyViolationError,\n  RepositoryRelativeFile,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\n\nconst repositoryRootUrl = new URL(\"../..\", import.meta.url);\nconst TrackedFileInventory = Schema.Array(RepositoryRelativeFile);\n\nexport const checkRepositoryPaths = (repositoryRoot: string) =>\n  Effect.gen(function* checkTrackedRepositoryText() {\n    const childProcesses = yield* ChildProcessSpawner.ChildProcessSpawner;\n    const fileSystem = yield* FileSystem.FileSystem;\n    const path = yield* Path.Path;\n\n    const inventory = yield* Effect.gen(function* listTrackedFiles() {\n      const handle = yield* childProcesses.spawn(\n        ChildProcess.make(\"git\", [\"ls-files\", \"-z\"], {\n          cwd: repositoryRoot,\n          extendEnv: true,\n          forceKillAfter: \"2 seconds\",\n          stderr: \"pipe\",\n          stdin: \"ignore\",\n          stdout: \"pipe\",\n        })\n      );\n      const [stdout, [exitCode]] = yield* Effect.all(\n        [\n          Stream.runCollect(handle.stdout),\n          Effect.zip(handle.exitCode, Stream.runDrain(handle.stderr), {\n            concurrent: true,\n          }),\n        ],\n        { concurrency: \"unbounded\" }\n      );\n\n      yield* Match.value(Number(exitCode)).pipe(\n        Match.when(0, () => Effect.void),\n        Match.orElse((code) =>\n          Effect.fail(\n            new RepositoryInventoryError({\n              exitCode: code,\n              operation: \"list-tracked-files\",\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      );\n\n      const bytes = Uint8Array.from(Array.flatMap(stdout, Array.fromIterable));\n      const decoded = yield* Effect.try({\n        catch: () =>\n          new RepositoryInventoryError({\n            operation: \"decode-tracked-files\",\n          }),\n        try: () => new TextDecoder(\"utf-8\", { fatal: true }).decode(bytes),\n      });\n\n      return yield* pipe(\n        decoded.split(\"\\0\"),\n        Array.filter((file) => file.length > 0),\n        Schema.decodeUnknownEffect(TrackedFileInventory),\n        Effect.mapError(\n          () =>\n            new RepositoryInventoryError({\n              operation: \"decode-tracked-files\",\n            })\n        )\n      );\n    }).pipe(\n      Effect.scoped,\n      Effect.catchTag(\"PlatformError\", () =>\n        Effect.fail(\n          new RepositoryInventoryError({\n            operation: \"list-tracked-files\",\n          })\n        )\n      )\n    );\n\n    const inspected = yield* Effect.forEach(\n      inventory,\n      (file) => {\n        const filePath = path.join(repositoryRoot, file);\n\n        return fileSystem.readLink(filePath).pipe(\n          Effect.map((target) => new TextEncoder().encode(target)),\n          Effect.catchTag(\"PlatformError\", () => fileSystem.readFile(filePath)),\n          Effect.mapError(() => new RepositoryFileReadError({ file })),\n          Effect.map((bytes) =>\n            decodeReadableRepositoryText(bytes).pipe(\n              Option.match({\n                onNone: () => ({ binary: true, findings: [] }),\n                onSome: (text) => ({\n                  binary: false,\n                  findings: inspectRepositoryText(file, text),\n                }),\n              })\n            )\n          )\n        );\n      },\n      { concurrency: 16 }\n    );\n    const binaryFiles = Array.filter(inspected, (file) => file.binary).length;\n\n    return createRepositoryPathReport({\n      binaryFiles,\n      findings: Array.flatMap(inspected, (file) => file.findings),\n      textFiles: inspected.length - binaryFiles,\n      trackedFiles: inventory.length,\n    });\n  });\n\nconst program = Effect.gen(function* repositoryPathMain() {\n  const path = yield* Path.Path;\n  const repositoryRoot = yield* path.fromFileUrl(repositoryRootUrl).pipe(\n    Effect.mapError(\n      () =>\n        new RepositoryInventoryError({\n          operation: \"resolve-repository-root\",\n        })\n    )\n  );\n\n  return yield* checkRepositoryPaths(repositoryRoot);\n}).pipe(\n  Effect.tap((report) => Console.info(renderRepositoryPathReport(report))),\n  Effect.tap((report) =>\n    Match.value(report.findings.length).pipe(\n      Match.when(0, () => Effect.void),\n      Match.orElse(() =>\n        Effect.fail(new RepositoryPolicyViolationError({ report }))\n      )\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryInventoryError\", (error) =>\n    Console.error(\n      `Repository path check failed during ${error.operation}${Option.fromNullishOr(\n        error.exitCode\n      ).pipe(\n        Option.match({\n          onNone: () => \"\",\n          onSome: (exitCode) => ` (exit ${exitCode})`,\n        })\n      )}.`\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryFileReadError\", (error) =>\n    Console.error(`Repository path check could not read ${error.file}.`)\n  ),\n  Effect.tapErrorTag(\"RepositoryPolicyViolationError\", () => Effect.void),\n  Effect.provide(BunServices.layer)\n);\n\nMatch.value(import.meta.main).pipe(\n  Match.when(true, () => BunRuntime.runMain(program)),\n  Match.orElse(() => false)\n);\n"},"started_at_ms":1791305993653,"completed_at_ms":1791305993653}}
