nly repository-relative file,\npositive line and closed finding category. Binary files are identified by a\nNUL byte or failed strict UTF-8 decode and skipped. For skill governance it\nalso runs `test:skills`, which validates required policy language and rejects\nstale provider-wrapper examples. The root graph also runs\n`check:harness-governance` exactly once. That Effect-native gate decodes the\nTaxKit profile, structured HE findings/crosswalk, canonical skill receipt, and\ncritical-journey inventory at filesystem ingress, then checks local skill-tree\ndigests, the two permitted profile overlays, the two declared extras, eight\nrelative Claude links, the maintained lifecycle with stable spec/plan index\nowners, self-contained references, portable runtime paths, and external\nnon-claims. Its positive and adversarial corpus is owned by\n`tools/governance/`; focused type and test commands are\n`check:harness-governance:types` and `test:harness-governance`.\nTarget-specific requalification is separately owned by\n`check:harness-foundation-epoch` and its focused TypeScript check. That command\nbinds one immutable candidate to complete validator sources, the canonical\nskill and journey projections, retained failures, five receipts, fresh\nindependent review, clocks, limitations and non-claims. It is a closeout check,\nnot another root-verification or Quality-workflow edge.\nFor docs, `apps/docs` type checking also\ntypechecks checked examples,\n# TaxKit documentation profile\n\nRead this profile after `AGENTS.md` and `docs/README.md`. Paths and commands\nbelow are repository-local; resolve the checkout with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`.\n\n## Owner map\n\n| Change class                                        | Earliest owner and required pointers                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Maintainer lifecycle, truth layers, archive routing | `docs/README.md`; architecture, standards, audit and active intent only when affected                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| Calculator rules, facts and schemas                 | owning `packages/calculators` or `packages/rules/**` source/README; relevant `docs/architecture/**`, SDK/API/public docs only when consumers change                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| SDK exports and examples                            | `packages/sdk/typescript` source/export map and README; packed-consumer/downstream proof; `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| HTTP/OpenAPI                                        | `packages/api/http/src/**` schemas and `src/openapi.ts`; generated snapshot `packages/api/http/__snapshots__/openapi.json` through `test:openapi`; `packages/api/http/README.md`, `apps/api/README.md`, and API/SDK architecture only when their contracts change                                                               |\n| Public MDX/navigation/lifecycle                     | `packages/docs-content/content/**`, `packages/docs-content/navigation.json`, and `tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; `published` requires one exact `public.statusDecision.acceptanceRecords` binding to a strict addressable record, with the durable lifecycle decision routed from `docs/documentation-audit/hgi-207/public-mdx-lifecycle.json` |\n| Public docs runtime/generated Fumadocs              | `apps/docs/README.md`, `packages/docs-content/source.config.ts`, `packages/docs-content/.source`, and `packages/docs-fumadocs`; regenerate/check through the owning commands and never hand-edit generated output                                                                                                               |\n| Package/app roots                                   | owning package/app README, package ownership architecture, root routes only when discoverability changes                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| Commands, CI, versioning and release readiness      | `package.json`, workflow/command owner, `docs/standards/versioning.md`, `docs/runbooks/README.md`, testing-quality architecture and proof owner                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Runbooks, authority, proof and history              | exactly five target-owned procedures routed by `docs/runbooks/README.md`; `docs/operations/authority-model.md`; `tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json`; sanitized `docs/evidence/releases/**`, `docs/evidence/deployments/**`, or dated `docs/documentation-audit/**`; preserve provenance and non-claims                             |\n| PRD and implementation                              | target SPEC, sibling tasks and active plan; local `prd-writer`, `prd-review`, `prd-implementer` invoke this skill                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n\nPublic `published` needs an exact accepted record and one-to-one binding in\n`tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; its `targetPath` must equal the public\npath. Navigation remains independently draft unless it receives its own exact\nrecord and binding.\nGenerated source is authoritative over checked output. Repository evidence is\nnot provider, registry, deployment, public-site or consumer proof.\n\n## Commands and boundaries\n\n- Baseline documentation/path/skill checks: `bun run test:skills`, `bun run\ncheck:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks`, `bun run check:repository-paths`.\n- Harness foundation checks: `bun run check:harness-governance:types`, `bun run\n  test:harness-governance`, and `bun run check:harness-governance`. The runtime\n  gate reads only repository-local profile, audit, receipt, skill, link, and\n  critical-journey owners.\n- Full local closeout: `bun run verification` and `git diff --check`.\n- Public content/runtime: `bun run docs:validate`, `bun run docs:build`,\n  `bun run --filter=docs test:browser` when applicable.\n- SDK package boundary: `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk check-packed-artifact`\n  and `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk validate:downstream` when applicable.\n- Release evidence: `bun run release:check` is local proof only; versioning,\n  publication and deployment remain separately authorized operations.\n- Runbook contract: `bun run check:runbooks` is inspect-only and writes the\n  bounded ignored `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`; it never runs a\n  documented procedure or establishes external state.\n\nFor each check, state its observable postcondition and what it does not prove.\nKeep background freshness reports as candidates until an attached implementation\nauthority, responsible reviewer and separately named publisher accept them.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7709},"formatted_output":"1603:    \"report\": \"# DEV-76 / CSF-T005 design documentation check\\n\\nDate: 7 October 2026. Mode: Read. Outcome: preserve the existing design.\\n\\nOnly this temporary report was written. No repository file, design guide,\\nprovider or public site was changed by this pass.\\n\\nThe new documentation pages extend the existing Website. The stylesheet at\\nHEAD and the working stylesheet have the same original 184 lines; the diff\\nonly adds document styles. The background, main text, font stack, top\\nnavigation, form styles and keyboard focus colour remain as they were.\\n\\n## Five-line system summary\\n\\n1. Palette: pale background (#f8fafc), dark text (#172033), quieter navigation text (#526071), light borders (#d6dde7), inherited blue focus (#2563eb), and document links in darker blue (#075985).\\n2. Type: the existing Inter/system font stack; article text (1.0625rem, line height 1.75); page title (clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem), line height 1.15); navigation and tables (0.9375rem); code blocks (0.875rem, line height 1.6).\\n3. Layout: article width capped at 72ch, meaning about 72 characters per line; a 17rem desktop sidebar; one column below 52rem; a native collapsible navigation list on phones.\\n4. Surfaces: plain background, thin borders, rounded code blocks (0.375rem), locally scrolling code and tables, and no added shadows or decorative imagery.\\n5. Named rules: no existing named visual rules were found and none were invented; preserve authored reading order, ordinary links, clear current-page marking and visible keyboard focus.\\n\\n## Evidence checked\\n\\nRepository root: `/Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit`.\\nBase HEAD: `049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e`.\\nThe checked artifact includes uncommitted work; HEAD alone does not identify it.\\n\\nThe operating instructions read were:\\n\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/document.md`, in full.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/agents/impeccable_documenter.toml`.\\n- `/Users/cooper/.agents/skills/impeccable/reference/degraded/documenter.md` for comparison with the shipped role. This pass used the actual delegated documenter role; no inline substitution was needed.\\n- The supplied repository `AGENTS.md` instructions, `docs/README.md`, `docs/architecture/frontend.md`, and the repository-local docs-maintainer skill, profile and its document-class, change-impact and proof references.\\n- Current documentation-route notes in `apps/web/README.md`, `docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md` and the active clean-slate plan.\\n\\nThe product source sampled was:\\n\\n| Source | SHA-256 at this pass | Observation |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `apps/web/src/styles.css` | `79c3834a0e88ff1a45a3cbfffef7fec11d740526e60c477d9a2334667e52eb83` | Compared with `git show HEAD:apps/web/src/styles.css` and its actual diff. All original rules are preserved; document rules are appended. |\\n| `apps/web/src/routes/$.tsx` | `3dd5b7088e0052b7976d5c671ba1ee3a9b38cfbe853cc0f8bc6f732659608610` | Sidebar and article remain visible in the route composition; loading, missing-page and unavailable states have clear copy; the article ends with a Markdown link. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/components.tsx` | `7a424f687699e4b672e5e6f5360e014594bc6efa6591966f3f84ac17b43182a5` | Internal page links retain navigation behaviour and deliberate heading focus. The table has a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll area. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/page.view.tsx` | `9ff7a422914f9da0d9d7909b7c77cfd24e931912fbb1b1fab6cbc417dc8f9b37` | Native details/summary navigation, checked page labels and explicit current-page marking. |\\n| `apps/web/src/lib/docs/mdx.boundary.tsx` | `7efcc5e0249fc5b258bf367f5354dd3d7ac3615b7763b9b802c0873d23218173` | Uses compiled authored pages, checks their text and metadata against the accepted page, and supplies fixed reload guidance for mismatches. |\\n\\nFour saved local captures were visually inspected. Their hashes match the\\ncurrent dated receipt:\\n\\n| Capture under `.alchemy/native-pair/screenshots/` | SHA-256 |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `docs-desktop.png` | `653b446948feaed665dc423cd2a9593d338fbbf4ecac0f283c15209c785e8a0c` |\\n| `docs-mobile.png` | `2d4e82cf3a7d43239eaf390a222953d31de7c77e82cf19bf1edf8e9be4babd5d` |\\n| `docs-diagram-desktop.png` | `34be2968577e465dbb8138f7a7398d1e6460c19a6d5bde8828085b69e0acb5fc` |\\n| `docs-diagram-mobile.png` | `d4afa74561abbc3dc530389551d1918e2f353766c7c8f05a1599772ff0df0e7b` |\\n\\nThe Quickstart and the \\u201cWhat are you changing?\\u201d page show their titles and\\nopening text at the top. The desktop sidebar, phone disclosure, underlined\\ndocument links, code blocks, table and keyboard focus match the source. No\\nblank or broken page region was observed in these captures.\\n\\nThe independent reviewer report at\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-finish-review.md` was read. Its SHA-256 is\\n`2742e01cd53393e748bfa1d9ca74b45b016621bb825dbc3f5898e6c07e07ef35`.\\nIt records `disposition: ship` and no material fixes for this reading and\\nnavigation extension.\\n\\nBefore reading product source, this pass checked\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-focus-a-results.jsonl`: `oxlint-tests` had\\nfinished with exit code 0. This respected the temporary source-replacement\\nwarning supplied with the task.\\n\\nThe saved native test log\\n`/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-native-l-native.log` records 7 passing test\\nfiles, 11 passing cases and exit code 0. This pass read that result; it did not\\nrerun the tests or operate a live browser. The dated source receipt at\\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json`\\nrecords 61 accepted pages, preserved navigation, retained integration\\ntemplates and retained calculator outputs. This design pass sampled two pages\\nand did not independently audit every content hash or tax result.\\n\\n## Documentation decision\\n\\n| Surface | Decision | Reason |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Existing Website visual system | Preserve | The original stylesheet is unchanged and the accepted brief requires an ordinary extension. |\\n| PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md and `.impeccable/design.json` | Preserve absence | A repository search found no matching design files. No new visual identity or system change was approved, so the documenter role does not require their creation. Missing files are context, not a failure. |\\n| Authored pages, navigation, examples and tax figures | Preserve | The supplied scope retains these owners; no content change was authorised for this pass. |\\n| Website README, frontend/content architecture and active T005 work | Preserve | These existing owners already describe the page connection and its unfinished work. This pass adds no durable implementation rule. |\\n| Generated references, API/SDK contract, release notes and Changesets | N/A | This pass changes no package, public contract, generator, version or release claim. |\\n| Runbooks, provider state, credentials, CI and publication | N/A | No operational action or external change is part of this pass. |\\n| This isolated evidence report | Change required | The delegated task explicitly requests a record of the design check at this exact temporary path. |\\n\\n## Limits and existing missing context\\n\\nNo PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, approved visual comp, quality card or approved system\\nchange was supplied. The incumbent source and explicit Read-mode extension\\nbrief give enough context for this check. No new brand metaphor, invented\\ndesign rule or replacement design file was introduced.\\n\\nThe diagram lettering is too small to read when fitted to the phone width.\\nThe readable table directly below gives the same choices and destinations;\\nthe reviewer accepted that solution. Small diagram lettering is recorded as a\\nlocal limitation, not a design rule for future pages to copy.\\n\\nThe dated receipt currently still calls full qualification and fresh review\\npending, while its embedded reviewer result says ship. This pre-existing\\nrecord mismatch was reported to the parent agent for the existing closeout\\nwork. It was not repaired by this read-only design pass. No other material\\nvisual drift was found in the sampled source or captures.\\n\\nSearch, discovery files, Markdown negotiation, share images and retirement of\\nthe old documentation app remain unfinished T005 work. Metrics remain\\ndeferred. This report establishes no deployment, public availability,\\npublication, complete repository qualification or external consumer result.\\n\\n```yaml\\ncandidate:\\n  source: The five sampled source files, incumbent HEAD stylesheet, four saved captures and named review/test records listed above.\\n  provenance: Delegated Impeccable documenter read-only comparison.\\n  freshness: Checked on 7 October 2026; source and capture hashes are listed above.\\n  classification: Supporting local design evidence; no system change.\\n  audience: Parent agent and Cooper.\\n  attachedEvidence: The exact source, capture, review and test paths listed above.\\n  proposedSemanticOwner: Existing Website source and frontend/content architecture; no new owner proposed.\\n  targetRevision: Base 049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e plus the sampled uncommitted source hashes above.\\n  unresolvedContradictions: Existing receipt says qualification/review pending while its embedded reviewer result says ship.\\n  responsibleReviewer: Parent agent for this supporting report; independent finish reviewer for the supplied ship decision.\\n  publisherIdentity: Unknown; no publication is requested or authorised by this pass.\\n  publicationStatus: Not published; isolated temporary report only.\\n  revocationQuarantine: Disregard this report if any sampled source changes; repeat the comparison before reuse.\\n  lastKnownGoodRecovery: Retain incumbent source; this pass has no repository mutation to roll back.\\n  postPublicationReadback: N/A; this pass performs no publication.\\n```\\n\\nNot made into a rule or repaired: the phone diagram's tiny text and the existing\\npending receipt wording, because this pass only records the accepted design\\nextension and leaves the owning closeout work with the parent agent.\\n\",\nRoot verification includes lint, format, both Knip graphs and workspace type\nchecks. Web compiler checking also includes Vite and both Vitest\nconfiguration owners. Its native package tests cover settings, safe error\nserialization and public build-input selection. Chromium retains two Atom\ncases and adds two actual file-route/generated-client cases: successful health\ndecoding and preload retirement that interrupts HTTP work and aborts its\nsignal. The fake transport is bounded browser-test proof; it is separate from\na built application or provider journey. The browser config pre-optimises the\nobserved imports so first-run dependency discovery cannot reload the test\niframe before assertions.\n The development-aware graph covers repository tooling, tests and\ncurrent application scaffolds. The production graph separately proves the\nnine code-bearing packages in the ten-artifact release closure,\n`@taxkit/scripts` exports and commands, and the standalone API runtime without\ntest or development reachability. It also models the real `apps/docs`,\n`@taxkit/docs-content` and `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs` production entries,\nincluding the generated browser/server source consumed by the app and the\nbuild-time Vite/source config. `@taxkit/tsconfig` is JSON-only and remains\ncovered by strict packed/downstream artifact proof rather than a fabricated\nTypeScript entrypoint. Root tools remain outside the production\ngraph by ownership. Root verification also typechecks and executes\nthe root repository-path gate, which scans\nGit-tracked readable text and safely reports only repository-relative file,\npositive line and closed finding category. Binary files are identified by a\nNUL byte or failed strict UTF-8 decode and skipped. For skill governance it\nalso runs `test:skills`, which validates required policy language and rejects\nstale provider-wrapper examples. The root graph also runs\n`check:harness-governance` exactly once. That Effect-native gate decodes the\nTaxKit profile, structured HE findings/crosswalk, canonical skill receipt, and\ncritical-journey inventory at filesystem ingress, then checks local skill-tree\ndigests, the two permitted profile overlays, the two declared extras, eight\nrelative Claude links, the maintained lifecycle with stable spec/plan index\nowners, self-contained references, portable runtime paths, and external\nnon-claims. Its positive and adversarial corpus is owned by\n`tools/governance/`; focused type and test commands are\n`check:harness-governance:types` and `test:harness-governance`.\nTarget-specific requalification is separately owned by\n`check:harness-foundation-epoch` and its focused TypeScript check. That command\nbinds one immutable candidate to complete validator sources, the canonical\nskill and journey projections, retained failures, five receipts, fresh\nindependent review, clocks, limitations and non-claims. It is a closeout check,\nnot another root-verification or Quality-workflow edge.\nFor docs, `apps/docs` type checking also\ntypechecks checked examples,\n# TaxKit documentation profile\n\nRead this profile after `AGENTS.md` and `docs/README.md`. Paths and commands\nbelow are repository-local; resolve the checkout with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`.\n\n## Owner map\n\n| Change class                                        | Earliest owner and required pointers                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Maintainer lifecycle, truth layers, archive routing | `docs/README.md`; architecture, standards, audit and active intent only when affected                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| Calculator rules, facts and schemas                 | owning `packages/calculators` or `packages/rules/**` source/README; relevant `docs/architecture/**`, SDK/API/public docs only when consumers change                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| SDK exports and examples                            | `packages/sdk/typescript` source/export map and README; packed-consumer/downstream proof; `docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md`                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| HTTP/OpenAPI                                        | `packages/api/http/src/**` schemas and `src/openapi.ts`; generated snapshot `packages/api/http/__snapshots__/openapi.json` through `test:openapi`; `packages/api/http/README.md`, `apps/api/README.md`, and API/SDK architecture only when their contracts change                                                               |\n| Public MDX/navigation/lifecycle                     | `packages/docs-content/content/**`, `packages/docs-content/navigation.json`, and `tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; `published` requires one exact `public.statusDecision.acceptanceRecords` binding to a strict addressable record, with the durable lifecycle decision routed from `docs/documentation-audit/hgi-207/public-mdx-lifecycle.json` |\n| Public docs runtime/generated Fumadocs              | `apps/docs/README.md`, `packages/docs-content/source.config.ts`, `packages/docs-content/.source`, and `packages/docs-fumadocs`; regenerate/check through the owning commands and never hand-edit generated output                                                                                                               |\n| Package/app roots                                   | owning package/app README, package ownership architecture, root routes only when discoverability changes                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| Commands, CI, versioning and release readiness      | `package.json`, workflow/command owner, `docs/standards/versioning.md`, `docs/runbooks/README.md`, testing-quality architecture and proof owner                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| Runbooks, authority, proof and history              | exactly five target-owned procedures routed by `docs/runbooks/README.md`; `docs/operations/authority-model.md`; `tools/documentation/runbook-contract.json`; sanitized `docs/evidence/releases/**`, `docs/evidence/deployments/**`, or dated `docs/documentation-audit/**`; preserve provenance and non-claims                             |\n| PRD and implementation                              | target SPEC, sibling tasks and active plan; local `prd-writer`, `prd-review`, `prd-implementer` invoke this skill                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n\nPublic `published` needs an exact accepted record and one-to-one binding in\n`tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`; its `targetPath` must equal the public\npath. Navigation remains independently draft unless it receives its own exact\nrecord and binding.\nGenerated source is authoritative over checked output. Repository evidence is\nnot provider, registry, deployment, public-site or consumer proof.\n\n## Commands and boundaries\n\n- Baseline documentation/path/skill checks: `bun run test:skills`, `bun run\ncheck:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks`, `bun run check:repository-paths`.\n- Harness foundation checks: `bun run check:harness-governance:types`, `bun run\n  test:harness-governance`, and `bun run check:harness-governance`. The runtime\n  gate reads only repository-local profile, audit, receipt, skill, link, and\n  critical-journey owners.\n- Full local closeout: `bun run verification` and `git diff --check`.\n- Public content/runtime: `bun run docs:validate`, `bun run docs:build`,\n  `bun run --filter=docs test:browser` when applicable.\n- SDK package boundary: `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk check-packed-artifact`\n  and `bun run --filter=@taxkit/sdk validate:downstream` when applicable.\n- Release evidence: `bun run release:check` is local proof only; versioning,\n  publication and deployment remain separately authorized operations.\n- Runbook contract: `bun run check:runbooks` is inspect-only and writes the\n  bounded ignored `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`; it never runs a\n  documented procedure or establishes external state.\n\nFor each check, state its observable postcondition and what it does not prove.\nKeep background freshness reports as candidates until an attached implementation\nauthority, responsible reviewer and separately named publisher accept them.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791306003222,"completed_at_ms":1791306003222}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:00:03.358Z","ordinal":48756,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7ee446c5-1aa4-4348-963d-10f94c2a6a47","process_id":"63529","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git status --short && sed -n '1,100p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short && sed -n '1,100p' docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"documentType\": \"bounded-proof-receipt\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"evidence\",\n  \"authority\": \"supporting\",\n  \"owner\": \"taxkit-web-app-owner\",\n  \"observedAt\": \"2026-10-06T16:48:08.600803+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"Local Website documentation page/navigation connection qualified; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n  \"baseHead\": \"049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e\",\n  \"actorAuthority\": {\n    \"principal\": \"Cooper\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex\",\n    \"operation\": \"Approved CSF-T005 implementation, local checks, commits, pushes and continuation of draft PR 155\",\n    \"environment\": \"Built local workerd/Chromium API and Website pair\",\n    \"approvalBoundary\": \"No merge, publication, deployment or provider apply\"\n  },\n  \"outcome\": [\n    \"The Website composes four named documentation operations over its private binding and renders 61 accepted pages through browser-safe compiled presentation.\",\n    \"The materialised native HTTP request preserves JSON byte bodies, binding receiver and signal; returned native Responses are immediately checked and provider diagnostics discarded.\",\n    \"The data-free native page GET carries only a bounded checked public header; original SSR pathnames determine page identity. Only generated settings/page URLs are admitted.\",\n    \"Dedicated route restoration precedes route-owned result matching and sidebar/article composition. Native missing pages return HTML 404; expected failures have fixed recoverable guidance.\",\n    \"Compiled Markdown and frontmatter must match the checked API page at preload and display. Three controlled cold native mismatches fail safely.\",\n    \"Internal links retain router navigation, deliberate heading focus, a unique current-page marker, phone disclosure, keyboard table scrolling and ordinary no-JavaScript reading.\"\n  ],\n  \"impact\": {\n    \"changeRequired\": [\n      \"Website app/client/config/native-loader/route/presentation/build ownership\",\n      \"Exact lint selectors and actual command fixtures\",\n      \"Website/content/RPC READMEs, frontend/API/content/package/testing architecture\",\n      \"SPEC/task/active-plan pointers, existing native critical journey and this receipt\",\n      \"Effect services architecture: the typed route context supplies both named settings/catalogue and documentation-page transports\"\n    ],\n    \"preserve\": [\n      \"61 accepted authored pages, navigation, 64 historical review records, 62 active bindings and four integration templates\",\n      \"Calculator contract and retained tax outputs; Medicare decision remains unresolved\",\n      \"Historical docs app/procedures and immutable receipts\",\n      \"Disabled collection and explicit metrics deferral\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": [\n      \"No new runbook command or deployment/recovery operation: existing local native procedure is extended\",\n      \"No new Changeset: private app consumers/tests only; existing package contract Changeset retained\",\n      \"No provider/credentials/registry/publication/CI workflow change\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"priorFailureAndRecovery\": [\n    \"Actual cold mismatch SSR first failed through a request body stream associated with an earlier Cloudflare request. The generic installed Fetcher adapter creates that stream; installed Effect HttpClientRequest.toWeb preserves the original bytes. The app now uses that native conversion and attached binding fetch. Fresh native mismatches return safe HTML and checked errors. No dependency upgrade or alternate RPC protocol was introduced.\",\n    \"A naive browser-code canary matched PublicCalculatorService.calculate in accepted public documentation prose. The test now positively requires @taxkit/calculators/PublicCalculatorService in the actual API bundle and excludes that executable Context identity from browser output.\",\n    \"TanStack parent-route link activation produced more than one current-page marker; exact link matching restores unique page semantics.\",\n    \"Earlier test locators used a guessed SDK address and an absent authored link. They now select the actual accepted /sdk/typescript-sdk and Plain SDK destinations; no source content was changed.\",\n    \"The first diagram desktop screenshot retained mobile table-focus scroll position. All four supplemental captures now explicitly start at document top.\",\n    \"First full verification passed all32 real workflow checks but stopped at Knip: WebsiteDocsPageView was exported despite being used only within its owning Schema module. It is now private; no runtime shape or external package contract changed. The complete corrected qualification is separate from that failed attempt.\",\n    \"Second full verification passed workflow/Knip/types but stopped before standalone browser assertions: the route tree followed the docs route static loader import into Cloudflare and native server-only code. Application getRouter now supplies the named page loader through the existing typed RouterContext pattern beside settings. The page route imports no loader implementation. Focused standalone browser tests pass all20 cases without aliases, mocks of server modules or an extra compiler plugin; native production transport proof remains separate.\"\n  ],\n  \"focusedChecks\": [\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"format\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"run\",\n        \"format\"\n      ],\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"durationSeconds\": 0.62,\n      \"log\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-native-l-format.log\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"native\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"run\",\n        \"--filter=web\",\n        \"test:native-pair\"\n      ],\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"durationSeconds\": 90.43,\n      \"log\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-native-l-native.log\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"install\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"install\"\n      ],\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"durationSeconds\": 0.38,\n      \"log\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-focus-a-install.log\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"format\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"bun\",\n        \"run\",\n        \"format\"\n      ],\n      \"exitCode\": 0,\n      \"durationSeconds\": 0.6,\n      \"log\": \"/private/tmp/dev76-website-docs-focus-a-format.log\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage\": \"web-types\",\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"documentType\": \"bounded-proof-receipt\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"evidence\",\n  \"authority\": \"supporting\",\n  \"owner\": \"taxkit-web-app-owner\",\n  \"observedAt\": \"2026-10-06T16:48:08.600803+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"Local Website documentation page/navigation connection qualified; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n  \"baseHead\": \"049b04ff9b71e8705507e819ba3ea31f8c9fa64e\",\n  \"actorAuthority\": {\n    \"principal\": \"Cooper\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex\",\n    \"operation\": \"Approved CSF-T005 implementation, local checks, commits, pushes and continuation of draft PR 155\",\n    \"environment\": \"Built local workerd/Chromium API and Website pair\",\n    \"approvalBoundary\": \"No merge, publication, deploym